1
00:00:02,190 --> 00:00:07,168
The Life Of Muhammad ﷺ, Madinan Period Volume 2

2
00:00:07,711 --> 00:00:09,705
By Imam Anwar Al_Awlaki,

3
00:00:10,319 --> 00:00:12,521
اَعُوْذُ بِاللهِ مِنَّ الشِّيْطَانِ الرَّجِيْمِ ۝ بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيْمَ۝

4
00:00:12,570 --> 00:00:17,866
اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرا

5
00:00:18,478 --> 00:00:19,575
Dear brothers and sisters,

6
00:00:19,600 --> 00:00:21,578
السلام وعليكم ورحمة الله وبركاته

7
00:00:22,145 --> 00:00:29,839
We have one topic left from the topic of the Battle of Tabook(تبوك),

8
00:00:30,757 --> 00:00:34,469
and this is the, what is known as the Hadith(حديث) of Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك).

9
00:00:34,926 --> 00:00:38,094
It's an authentic narration from him, narrated by Al-Bukhari(البخاريْ)

10
00:00:38,708 --> 00:00:42,023
and by other books of Hadith(حديث) and books of Seerah(سيرة).

11
00:00:43,033 --> 00:00:45,331
This Hadith(حديث) has special significance

12
00:00:45,694 --> 00:00:56,620
because it represents a bad moment in the life of an exemplary man, special man, the companion of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

13
00:00:57,140 --> 00:01:00,116
 and it's loaded with lessons for us.

14
00:01:00,739 --> 00:01:06,746
Because it is a story of someone, who struggled to do good,

15
00:01:07,484 --> 00:01:11,999
and then being a human being, he went through a moment of weakness

16
00:01:12,567 --> 00:01:16,939
but was able to get out of it because of his good deeds,

17
00:01:17,270 --> 00:01:19,839
because of his Tarbiyyah(تربية), because of his Eeman(إيمان).

18
00:01:20,399 --> 00:01:26,184
And I want you to contemplate on this Hadith(حديث), deeply

19
00:01:26,407 --> 00:01:30,375
and derive the lessons that are relevant to you, as a Mo'min(مؤمن),

20
00:01:30,929 --> 00:01:35,849
we'll go In Sha Allah(إن شاء الله) through some of these lessons, but I'm sure that I would miss many.

21
00:01:36,403 --> 00:01:45,286
And therefore you need to have Tadabbur(تدبر), contemplation on these words of the great companion Ka'ab Ibn Malik رضي الله عنه.

22
00:01:45,788 --> 00:01:48,048
I'm going to read the narration of Bukhari(بخاريْ)

23
00:01:48,319 --> 00:01:52,669
and this was narrated by the grandson of Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك) from his father,

24
00:01:52,693 --> 00:01:58,800
who was the guide of Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك), when he grew old and became blind

25
00:01:59,630 --> 00:02:03,457
and the father is narrating his story to the son.

26
00:02:03,497 --> 00:02:04,768
Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك) says;

27
00:02:04,958 --> 00:02:11,802
لَمْ أَتَخَلَّفْ عَنْ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي غَزْوَةٍ غَزَاهَا إِلَّا فِي غَزْوَةِ تَبُوكَ

28
00:02:12,294 --> 00:02:19,526
Ka'ab(كعب) says: I've never stayed behind any Battle of Rasool Allah ﷺ

29
00:02:19,976 --> 00:02:22,451
with the exception of the Battle of Tabook(تبوك).

30
00:02:23,041 --> 00:02:25,535
غَيْرَ أَنِّي كُنْتُ تَخَلَّفْتُ فِي غَزْوَةِ بَدْرٍ

31
00:02:26,328 --> 00:02:28,570
But I also missed the Battle of Badr(بدر).

32
00:02:28,649 --> 00:02:29,424
However,

33
00:02:29,527 --> 00:02:31,687
وَلَمْ يُعَاتِبْ أَحَدًا تَخَلَّفَ عَنْهَا

34
00:02:32,110 --> 00:02:36,158
Rasool Allah ﷺ did not censor anybody who stayed behind.

35
00:02:36,182 --> 00:02:41,556
And he gives the reason why, Rasool Allah ﷺ did not hold anybody accountable for missing Badr(بدر).?

36
00:02:41,816 --> 00:02:44,929
إِنَّمَا خَرَجَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يُرِيدُ عِيرَ قُرَيْشٍ

37
00:02:45,648 --> 00:02:49,351
Rasool Allah ﷺ went out in the Battle of Badr(بدر) with a different intention.

38
00:02:49,375 --> 00:02:53,772
I mean, it wasn't intended as a Battle with the Mushrikeen(مشركين) of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ),

39
00:02:53,796 --> 00:03:00,599
but it was intended as an attack on the Tijarah(تجارة), on the caravan that was led by Abu Sufiyan(ابو سفيان),

40
00:03:00,999 --> 00:03:04,078
they missed the caravan and then they ended up meeting the army of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

41
00:03:04,640 --> 00:03:07,757
حَتَّى جَمَعَ اللَّهُ بَيْنَهُمْ وَبَيْنَ عَدُوِّهِمْ عَلَى غَيْرِ مِيعَادٍ

42
00:03:08,292 --> 00:03:13,583
And then, they ended up meeting the enemy without an appointment, a prior appointment.

43
00:03:14,096 --> 00:03:16,961
وَلَقَدْ شَهِدْتُ مَعَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ لَيْلَةَ الْعَقَبَةِ

44
00:03:17,492 --> 00:03:21,836
حِينَ تَوَاثَقْنَا عَلَى الْإِسْلَامِ وَمَا أُحِبُّ أَنَّ لِي بِهَا

45
00:03:22,051 --> 00:03:25,929
مَشْهَدَ بَدْرٍ وَإِنْ كَانَتْ بَدْرٌ أَذْكَرَ فِي النَّاسِ مِنْهَا

46
00:03:26,660 --> 00:03:33,520
He says: However, I have attended with Rasool Allah ﷺ the night of Al-Aqabah(ألعقبه).

47
00:03:34,149 --> 00:03:40,735
Remember, we have talked about Al-Aqabah(ألعقبه) towards the end of the series on Makkah.

48
00:03:41,332 --> 00:03:47,275
And this is when the Ansaar(أنْصَار) gave Rasool Allah ﷺ the Pledge of Allegiance

49
00:03:47,897 --> 00:03:49,896
and they promised him support.

50
00:03:50,308 --> 00:03:53,697
Ka'ab(كعب) says: I attended that, he was one of the Nuqaba'a(نقباء),

51
00:03:53,896 --> 00:03:58,139
he was one of the 12 leaders of Al-Ansaar(أنْصَار),

52
00:03:58,506 --> 00:04:04,130
who represented the Ansaar(أنْصَار) in giving the pledge to Rasool Allah ﷺ.

53
00:04:04,650 --> 00:04:11,420
Ka'ab(كعب) says, that I would not want to have attended Badr(بدر) instead of Al-Aqabah(ألعقبه),

54
00:04:11,783 --> 00:04:13,560
even though Badr(بدر) is more famous.

55
00:04:13,876 --> 00:04:16,309
What Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك) is saying,

56
00:04:16,635 --> 00:04:22,268
 that they consider the night of Al-Aqabah(العقبه) to be such an important and special event

57
00:04:22,563 --> 00:04:25,620
that he would not exchange it, with attending Badr(بدر).

58
00:04:26,139 --> 00:04:30,072
But then he says, that Badr(بدر) is very famous and it has such a high reputation.

59
00:04:30,421 --> 00:04:38,764
However, the Laila-Tul-Aqabah(ليلة العقبه) was also a very important event and he attended that, he was there.

60
00:04:39,455 --> 00:04:40,234
And then he says;

61
00:04:40,375 --> 00:04:48,178
كَانَ مِنْ خَبَرِي أَنِّي لَمْ أَكُنْ قَطُّ أَقْوَى وَلَا أَيْسَرَ حِينَ تَخَلَّفْتُ عَنْهُ فِي تِلْكَ الْغَزَاةِ

62
00:04:48,314 --> 00:04:54,043
وَاللَّهِ مَا اجْتَمَعَتْ عِنْدِي قَبْلَهُ رَاحِلَتَانِ قَطُّ حَتَّى جَمَعْتُهُمَا فِي تِلْكَ الْغَزْوَةِ

63
00:04:54,461 --> 00:04:59,898
He said: And now he's starting to narrate the story of what happened on Tabook(تبوك).

64
00:05:00,113 --> 00:05:05,283
He said: I was never before stronger or better off,

65
00:05:05,725 --> 00:05:09,478
then that time when I missed the Battle of Tabook(تبوك).

66
00:05:09,502 --> 00:05:14,680
He said: Never before, did I own two riding camels.

67
00:05:15,614 --> 00:05:18,846
But I did own them during the Battle of Tabook(تبوك).

68
00:05:19,421 --> 00:05:23,505
So, Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك) here is admitting that he has no excuse,

69
00:05:24,062 --> 00:05:28,510
he's strong, and he has a financial capability,

70
00:05:28,899 --> 00:05:35,696
which is represented in having a mount to ride, not only did he have one but he had two.

71
00:05:36,378 --> 00:05:42,539
وَلَمْ يَكُنْ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يُرِيدُ غَزْوَةً إِلَّا وَرَّى بِغَيْرِهَا

72
00:05:43,114 --> 00:05:48,196
حَتَّى كَانَتْ تِلْكَ الْغَزْوَةُ غَزَاهَا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي حَرٍّ شَدِيدٍ

73
00:05:48,598 --> 00:05:53,266
وَاسْتَقْبَلَ سَفَرًا بَعِيدًا وَمَفَازًا وَعَدُوًّا كَثِيرًا

74
00:05:53,396 --> 00:06:00,733
فَجَلَّى لِلْمُسْلِمِينَ أَمْرَهُمْ لِيَتَأَهَّبُوا أُهْبَةَ غَزْوِهِمْ فَأَخْبَرَهُمْ بِوَجْهِهِ الَّذِي يُرِيدُ

75
00:06:01,086 --> 00:06:07,748
Rasool Allah ﷺ would never send out an army to fight a particular enemy.

76
00:06:08,170 --> 00:06:11,886
But he would talk about a different destination.

77
00:06:12,461 --> 00:06:14,929
Rasool Allah ﷺ does this to mislead the enemy,

78
00:06:15,347 --> 00:06:19,600
so he would never have, his destination exposed.

79
00:06:19,895 --> 00:06:24,816
And he would do that in order to surprise the enemy and catch them, off guard.

80
00:06:25,311 --> 00:06:28,148
That was the habit of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

81
00:06:28,461 --> 00:06:31,392
However, with the Battle of Tabook(تبوك), it was different.

82
00:06:31,779 --> 00:06:35,586
Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك) says; Because it was in a time of extreme heat,

83
00:06:36,231 --> 00:06:40,369
and it was a long journey and it was a numerous enemy,

84
00:06:40,615 --> 00:06:46,340
therefore, Rasool Allah ﷺ made the announcement public to the Muslims,

85
00:06:46,711 --> 00:06:52,234
that we are going to such and such place, and we are facing the Romans.

86
00:06:52,690 --> 00:06:59,057
And he did that so that they will take appropriate measures and preparations for this battle.

87
00:06:59,579 --> 00:07:03,112
So, this shows you that Tabook(تبوك) was different and special.

88
00:07:03,903 --> 00:07:10,298
وَالْمُسْلِمُونَ مَعَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ كَثِيرٌ، وَلَا يَجْمَعُهُمْ كِتَابٌ حَافِظٌ يُرِيدُ الدِّيوَانَ

89
00:07:10,572 --> 00:07:16,325
The Muslims were numerous and the books of Seerah(سيرة) say that they were 30,000.

90
00:07:16,602 --> 00:07:20,196
That is the most authentic narration that the number of Muslims was 30,000.

91
00:07:20,416 --> 00:07:24,986
So, you can see that it surpasses any other battle before it.

92
00:07:25,066 --> 00:07:31,299
I mean, in Fattah-e-Makkah(فتح مكه), they were 10, and in Hawazin(هوازن), they were 12,000.

93
00:07:31,323 --> 00:07:40,310
And now suddenly, we have a jump to 30,000 even though it's just a few months after the Battle of Hawazin(هوازن),

94
00:07:40,608 --> 00:07:45,597
but Rasool Allah ﷺ made a full mobilization for the Battle of Tabook(تبوك),

95
00:07:45,629 --> 00:07:50,465
and all of the tribes were called to, and summoned to attend,

96
00:07:50,813 --> 00:07:53,584
because again, of the special circumstances.

97
00:07:54,588 --> 00:07:56,853
Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك) says: But there is no Deewan(ديوان).

98
00:07:56,893 --> 00:08:02,263
Deewan(ديوان) is a register, meaning the names, there was no role, the names were not written.

99
00:08:02,589 --> 00:08:04,057
And therefore he says;

100
00:08:04,256 --> 00:08:07,250
فَمَا رَجُلٌ يُرِيدُ أَنْ يَتَغَيَّبَ إِلَّا ظَنَّ أَنْ سَيَخْفَى

101
00:08:07,673 --> 00:08:14,384
So, if a person wants to stay behind, he might assume that he would be undisclosed.

102
00:08:14,849 --> 00:08:16,839
 مَا لَمْ يَنْزِلْ فِيهِ وَحْيُ مِنَّ اللَّهِ

103
00:08:16,863 --> 00:08:20,942
As long as there will be no revelation coming from Allah, exposing him.

104
00:08:21,298 --> 00:08:27,114
Because of the huge numbers a person could assume that Rasool Allah ﷺ would not miss that person.

105
00:08:27,283 --> 00:08:31,497
Because we're talking about 30,000 it's difficult to keep track of who's there and who's not.

106
00:08:31,986 --> 00:08:38,577
وَغَزَا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ تِلْكَ الْغَزْوَةَ حِينَ طَابَتْ الثِّمَارُ وَالظِّلَالُ

107
00:08:39,050 --> 00:08:40,371
Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك) says;

108
00:08:40,622 --> 00:08:52,911
And Rasool Allah ﷺ went out in that battle, in a time when the fruits were ripe, and the shade was alluring.

109
00:08:53,340 --> 00:08:57,076
And this is a very important statement of Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك).

110
00:08:57,385 --> 00:09:01,498
Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك) here is being honest, in this narration,

111
00:09:01,721 --> 00:09:07,837
and he is speaking to us about the true reasons, and the hidden reasons

112
00:09:08,274 --> 00:09:10,857
that are going within the mind and the heart.

113
00:09:11,774 --> 00:09:14,386
He is saying that, at that time,

114
00:09:14,851 --> 00:09:19,789
it was a time when the shade was very alluring because it was very hot,

115
00:09:20,337 --> 00:09:24,901
and the fruit are ripening on the trees.

116
00:09:25,163 --> 00:09:29,843
And these are temptations for a person to stay behind.

117
00:09:30,411 --> 00:09:31,296
And then he says;

118
00:09:31,666 --> 00:09:36,466
وَتَجَهَّزَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَالْمُسْلِمُونَ مَعَهُ

119
00:09:36,845 --> 00:09:43,506
فَطَفِقْتُ أَغْدُو لِكَيْ أَتَجَهَّزَ مَعَهُمْ فَأَرْجِعُ وَلَمْ أَقْضِ شَيْئًا فَأَقُولُ فِي نَفْسِي أَنَا قَادِرٌ عَلَيْهِ

120
00:09:44,131 --> 00:09:50,194
He said: The Messenger of Allah and the Muslims started making their preparations.

121
00:09:50,617 --> 00:09:55,651
And I began hurrying to prepare, but I would retire without accomplishing anything.

122
00:09:55,937 --> 00:09:59,259
He had the intention to prepare, but he would not do anything.

123
00:09:59,927 --> 00:10:05,770
Procrastination, a human habit, something that is usual, if you don't commit yourself,

124
00:10:05,795 --> 00:10:09,168
if you don't discipline yourself to do something, you're not going to do it.

125
00:10:09,484 --> 00:10:12,251
And you're going to delay the work of today to tomorrow.

126
00:10:12,670 --> 00:10:16,315
And that is what Ka'ab Ibn Malik رضي الله عنه was doing.

127
00:10:16,593 --> 00:10:18,382
And then he tells us something, he said;

128
00:10:18,406 --> 00:10:20,476
فَأَقُولُ فِي نَفْسِي أَنَا قَادِرٌ عَلَيْهِ

129
00:10:20,910 --> 00:10:24,429
I would tell myself that I'm able to do it.

130
00:10:24,874 --> 00:10:30,810
Nafs(نفس), the self could drag you down.

131
00:10:30,967 --> 00:10:32,206
If you don't discipline it.

132
00:10:32,662 --> 00:10:38,528
If you leave your affairs to your whims, and just let it go with the flow,

133
00:10:39,399 --> 00:10:41,012
you're not going to get anything done.

134
00:10:41,701 --> 00:10:45,712
And Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك) was speaking to himself and saying I can do it.

135
00:10:46,229 --> 00:10:47,732
Eventually he didn't do it.

136
00:10:48,034 --> 00:10:50,455
So, we need to be very careful from the Nafs(نفس)

137
00:10:50,712 --> 00:10:58,799
because the Nafs(نفس) is lazy, the Nafs(نفس) is afraid, the Nafs(نفس) is weak, the Nafs(نفس) loves Duniyah(دنيا).

138
00:10:59,019 --> 00:11:06,052
And if you don't force it, and discipline it and tame it to follow the orders of Allahعَزّوجَلّ,

139
00:11:06,142 --> 00:11:08,622
it will wonder with you and take you astray.

140
00:11:09,240 --> 00:11:14,937
You have to be very careful. Your Nafs(نفس) could be your worst enemy, if you don't pay attention.

141
00:11:15,562 --> 00:11:19,422
فَلَمْ يَزَلْ يَتَمَادَى بِي حَتَّى اشْتَدَّ بِالنَّاسِ الْجِدُّ

142
00:11:19,950 --> 00:11:25,449
فَأَصْبَحَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَالْمُسْلِمُونَ مَعَهُ وَلَمْ أَقْضِ مِنْ جَهَازِي شَيْئًا

143
00:11:26,080 --> 00:11:29,468
He said: ِ And time was passing by.

144
00:11:29,999 --> 00:11:33,698
And people were deep in their preparation.

145
00:11:34,196 --> 00:11:39,393
And then suddenly, the next morning Rasool Allah ﷺ, and the Muslims were ready.

146
00:11:39,741 --> 00:11:41,442
That's it, they're set to go.

147
00:11:41,633 --> 00:11:43,292
وَلَمْ أَقْضِ مِنْ جَهَازِي شَيْئًا

148
00:11:43,316 --> 00:11:45,837
And I have done nothing to prepare myself.

149
00:11:46,421 --> 00:11:53,489
He is at the initial stage, he has done nothing and the Muslims are ready to leave this morning.

150
00:11:53,596 --> 00:11:57,218
فَقُلْتُ أَتَجَهَّزُ بَعْدَهُ بِيَوْمٍ أَوْ يَوْمَيْنِ ثُمَّ أَلْحَقُهُمْ

151
00:11:57,574 --> 00:12:02,965
I said: I'm gonna prepare, get ready within a day or two, and then I'm going to catch up with them.

152
00:12:03,181 --> 00:12:07,909
فَغَدَوْتُ بَعْدَ أَنْ فَصَلُوا لِأَتَجَهَّزَ فَرَجَعْتُ وَلَمْ أَقْضِ شَيْئًا

153
00:12:08,013 --> 00:12:11,797
They left and I decided to get myself ready and I didn't.

154
00:12:11,981 --> 00:12:13,414
ثُمَّ غَدَوْتُ ثُمَّ رَجَعْتُ

155
00:12:13,438 --> 00:12:16,377
The next day, the same thing, I would come back and I would do nothing.

156
00:12:16,609 --> 00:12:19,203
فَلَمْ يَزَلْ بِي حَتَّى أَسْرَعُوا وَتَفَارَطَ الْغَزْوُ

157
00:12:19,536 --> 00:12:24,284
And that was the case, until the army has left and it was over.

158
00:12:25,054 --> 00:12:34,643
And here brothers and sisters, if you think that you could hasten a thing, so you procrastinate.

159
00:12:34,768 --> 00:12:37,239
And then you think that you can combine it and hasten it,

160
00:12:37,264 --> 00:12:40,676
many times what happens is, you end up doing nothing,

161
00:12:41,028 --> 00:12:46,735
because the issue piles up and piles up, until it becomes too much to manage.

162
00:12:47,164 --> 00:12:53,950
And it ends up causing you, when you look at the amount of work that you have to do, you just end up giving up.

163
00:12:54,248 --> 00:13:02,414
So, it's a trick from yourself to tell you to procastinate and then its another trick from yourself when yourself that's it, it's too late,

164
00:13:02,790 --> 00:13:05,216
and you end up, giving up.

165
00:13:06,065 --> 00:13:10,590
Also brothers and sisters, this is another indication because here

166
00:13:10,882 --> 00:13:15,422
Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك) is talking about of the context of going out Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

167
00:13:15,614 --> 00:13:22,237
Going out Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله) is a caravan and this caravan is moving and it's going on continuously

168
00:13:22,277 --> 00:13:23,776
 because Rasool Allah ﷺ says,

169
00:13:23,991 --> 00:13:26,362
That this will continue until the day of judgment.

170
00:13:27,390 --> 00:13:30,610
There will be an enemy that is fought at any point of time.

171
00:13:30,792 --> 00:13:33,329
According to the Ahadith(احاديث) of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

172
00:13:33,481 --> 00:13:36,221
the Ahadith(احاديث) of At-Taefa Al-Mansoorah(طائفه المنصورة) Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

173
00:13:36,245 --> 00:13:40,232
They are fighting, until the end of time, until Dajjal(دجال) comes out.

174
00:13:40,381 --> 00:13:42,152
And they will be fighting Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

175
00:13:42,476 --> 00:13:44,323
There was fighting Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله) yesterday,

176
00:13:44,498 --> 00:13:46,116
there is fighting Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله) today,

177
00:13:46,371 --> 00:13:48,411
and they will be fighting Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله) tomorrow

178
00:13:48,966 --> 00:13:50,568
and the caravan is moving,

179
00:13:50,862 --> 00:13:57,371
and the more you delay joining it, the further it will be and the more difficult it will be for you to catch up.

180
00:13:58,027 --> 00:14:00,521
And this is exactly what happened with Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك).

181
00:14:00,846 --> 00:14:04,334
If Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك) was not able and he failed to catch up.

182
00:14:04,439 --> 00:14:09,404
Who do you think, you are to be able to catch up, if you wait for too long.?

183
00:14:09,920 --> 00:14:10,880
And then he says;

184
00:14:10,970 --> 00:14:15,985
وَهَمَمْتُ أَنْ أَرْتَحِلَ فَأُدْرِكَهُمْ وَلَيْتَنِي فَعَلْتُ

185
00:14:16,327 --> 00:14:23,810
He said: And I was still thinking about setting out and catching up with them.

186
00:14:23,996 --> 00:14:26,013
And I wish that I did.

187
00:14:27,017 --> 00:14:32,595
Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك) wishes that he did and one day, you will wish that you did,

188
00:14:32,912 --> 00:14:35,058
if not in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) than in Aakhira(آخرة)

189
00:14:35,390 --> 00:14:39,409
when you see the great rewards that are given to these special people

190
00:14:39,530 --> 00:14:42,720
whom Allahعَزّوجَلّ has bestowed his favor upon

191
00:14:42,990 --> 00:14:48,736
and guided them to the straight path and showed them the best of deeds, the peak and pinnacle of Islam.

192
00:14:49,490 --> 00:14:53,722
You will desire that you did Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك) is saying; Laiytaani(لَيْتَنِي) I wish,

193
00:14:54,124 --> 00:14:55,370
I wish, that I did.

194
00:14:55,640 --> 00:14:57,331
فَلَمْ يُقَدَّرْ لِي ذَلِكَ

195
00:14:57,593 --> 00:14:59,799
It was not destined for me to do so.

196
00:15:00,639 --> 00:15:06,459
فَكُنْتُ إِذَا خَرَجْتُ فِي النَّاسِ بَعْدَ خُرُوجِ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ

197
00:15:06,628 --> 00:15:16,024
فَطُفْتُ فِيهِمْ أَحْزَنَنِي أَنِّي لَا أَرَى إِلَّا رَجُلًا مَغْمُوصًا عَلَيْهِ النِّفَاقُ أَوْ رَجُلًا مِمَّنْ عَذَرَ اللَّهُ مِنْ الضُّعَفَاءِ

198
00:15:16,761 --> 00:15:21,209
When the army left and he was left behind in Madina,

199
00:15:21,612 --> 00:15:24,522
he would go out, walk around, go to the marketplaces.

200
00:15:24,744 --> 00:15:28,002
He said: Whenever I went out and mixed with people,

201
00:15:28,467 --> 00:15:32,618
after the departure of the Messenger of Allah, it grieved me

202
00:15:33,005 --> 00:15:38,119
that the only man I saw were persons suspected of hypocrisy,

203
00:15:38,349 --> 00:15:43,165
or those excused by the Messenger of Allah because they were in poor health.

204
00:15:43,699 --> 00:15:48,896
So, these are the ones, who stay behind the Munafiqeen(منافقين) and the ones, who are excused.

205
00:15:49,350 --> 00:15:50,998
These are the ones who stay behind.

206
00:15:51,432 --> 00:15:56,306
وَلَمْ يَذْكُرْنِي رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ حَتَّى بَلَغَ تَبُوكَ

207
00:15:56,842 --> 00:16:00,519
The Messenger of Allah made no mention of me, until after he reached Tabook(تبوك).

208
00:16:00,544 --> 00:16:03,026
Rasool Allah remembered him, when he was at Tabook(تبوك).

209
00:16:03,507 --> 00:16:07,648
فَقَالَ وَهُوَ جَالِسٌ فِي الْقَوْمِ بِتَبُوكَ مَا فَعَلَ كَعْبٌ

210
00:16:08,168 --> 00:16:12,257
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: When he was in a gathering. What did Ka'ab(كعب) do?

211
00:16:12,933 --> 00:16:14,827
فَقَالَ رَجُلٌ مِنْ بَنِي سَلِمَةَ

212
00:16:15,292 --> 00:16:17,523
A man from Banni Salamah(بني سلمه) said;

213
00:16:17,761 --> 00:16:22,715
يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ حَبَسَهُ بُرْدَاهُ وَنَظَرُهُ فِي عِطْفِهِ

214
00:16:23,250 --> 00:16:28,517
This man from Bannu Salamah(بنو سلمه), the same clan of Ka'ab(كعب) from Al-Khazraj(الخزرج),

215
00:16:29,022 --> 00:16:34,464
he said: O Messenger of Allah, he was detained by his two cloaks

216
00:16:34,926 --> 00:16:38,017
and looking at the beauty of his clothes.

217
00:16:38,226 --> 00:16:45,188
Now, brothers and sisters, this is such a degrading statement that was made.

218
00:16:45,474 --> 00:16:47,969
I mean, here you're talking about men.

219
00:16:48,335 --> 00:16:51,872
They are True men, and they know what is shameful

220
00:16:51,912 --> 00:16:57,393
and such a statement is such a degrading statement against Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك)

221
00:16:58,053 --> 00:17:03,423
and to say that he was held behind because of his clothes and staring at them.

222
00:17:03,656 --> 00:17:06,018
I mean, he's like saying that, he is a woman,

223
00:17:06,398 --> 00:17:11,128
who just is enjoying her clothes and looking at how beautiful these clothes are.

224
00:17:11,406 --> 00:17:18,344
It's not a manly thing to be concerned with how cute the clothes are

225
00:17:18,433 --> 00:17:24,335
and how handsome a man looks in the mirror when people are fighting, when people are in the battlefield.

226
00:17:24,557 --> 00:17:26,852
So, it is a very shameful thing

227
00:17:27,228 --> 00:17:30,397
and Muadh Ibn Jabal(معاذ ابن جبل), who's also from Al-Ansaar(أنْصَار)

228
00:17:30,421 --> 00:17:34,931
and from the people of Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك), he responded to that statement and said;

229
00:17:35,372 --> 00:17:38,155
فَقَالَ مُعَاذُ بْنُ جَبَلٍ بِئْسَ مَا قُلْتَ

230
00:17:38,581 --> 00:17:40,824
What a bad thing you have said.

231
00:17:41,047 --> 00:17:44,578
وَاللَّهِ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ مَا عَلِمْنَا عَلَيْهِ إِلَّا خَيْرًا

232
00:17:44,602 --> 00:17:47,706
O Messenger of Allah. We know nothing about him but good.

233
00:17:48,063 --> 00:17:49,689
فَسَكَتَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ

234
00:17:49,713 --> 00:17:51,585
Rasool Allah ﷺ was quiet.

235
00:17:51,738 --> 00:17:57,727
Now, when Rasool Allah ﷺ is silent, that means that he is approving of what was mentioned

236
00:17:57,782 --> 00:18:03,180
otherwise, Rasool Allah ﷺ would answer back and let's take a look at this for a moment.

237
00:18:03,932 --> 00:18:05,144
Who is Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك).?

238
00:18:05,422 --> 00:18:09,937
Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك) is a man, who was with Rasool Allah ﷺ from day one.

239
00:18:10,504 --> 00:18:14,739
Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك) is a man, who is from among the Al-Ansaar(أنْصَار),

240
00:18:14,977 --> 00:18:18,305
who came to Rasool Allah ﷺ and invited him to Madina

241
00:18:18,606 --> 00:18:22,491
and they knew very well the consequences of such an act.

242
00:18:22,796 --> 00:18:25,327
They knew that the Arabs are going to fight them.

243
00:18:25,471 --> 00:18:31,541
They knew that they will sacrifice their selves, and their wealth for Rasool Allah ﷺ.

244
00:18:31,768 --> 00:18:37,172
And he is one of the 12 men, who put their hands in the hand of Rasool Allah ﷺ

245
00:18:37,270 --> 00:18:39,216
and gave him the Pledge of Allegiance.

246
00:18:39,455 --> 00:18:44,905
Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك) is a man, who was in the trench with Rasool Allah ﷺ in every day of battle,

247
00:18:44,985 --> 00:18:46,836
 he was there in Uhud(احد),

248
00:18:47,168 --> 00:18:48,383
he was there in Al-Khandaq(ألخندق),

249
00:18:48,639 --> 00:18:49,893
he was there in Fath-E-Makkah(فتح مكه),

250
00:18:50,043 --> 00:18:51,234
he was there Khaybar(خيبر),

251
00:18:51,307 --> 00:18:52,681
he was there Hudaybiyyah(حديبيه),

252
00:18:52,786 --> 00:18:56,358
he was there in every single important moment in the history of Islam,

253
00:18:56,557 --> 00:18:59,400
and he just missed out on that single day.

254
00:19:00,041 --> 00:19:03,324
Nevertheless, this man from Bannu Salamah(بنوسلمه)

255
00:19:03,421 --> 00:19:07,262
made that statement against him that he's staring at his clothes.

256
00:19:07,414 --> 00:19:14,095
So, brothers and sisters, the action of Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك) made him a target, to these words.

257
00:19:14,426 --> 00:19:19,131
I mean, he has put himself in a vulnerable position because of his actions.

258
00:19:19,596 --> 00:19:24,632
He did something that brought and drew these statements against him,

259
00:19:25,190 --> 00:19:30,322
even though he's such a good and great companion of Rasool Allah ﷺ

260
00:19:30,644 --> 00:19:35,611
but because what he did was wrong, he got himself into that situation.

261
00:19:36,035 --> 00:19:40,777
Regardless of whether the statement of this man is right or wrong.

262
00:19:41,008 --> 00:19:45,282
He, Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك) is the one, who put himself in this situation to start with

263
00:19:45,591 --> 00:19:50,073
and Muadh Ibn Jabal(معاذ ابن جبل) spoke in defense of Ka'ab Ibn Malik رضي الله عنه

264
00:19:50,251 --> 00:19:51,991
and Rasool Allah ﷺ was silent

265
00:19:52,229 --> 00:19:56,896
because Rasool Ullah صلوات الله وسلام عليه is taking by what is apparent.

266
00:19:56,936 --> 00:20:01,264
And what is apparent is that Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك) did not show up.

267
00:20:01,931 --> 00:20:03,735
And then Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك) says;

268
00:20:03,875 --> 00:20:10,021
قَالَ كَعْبُ بْنُ مَالِكٍ فَلَمَّا بَلَغَنِي أَنَّهُ تَوَجَّهَ قَافِلًا حَضَرَنِي هَمِّي

269
00:20:10,370 --> 00:20:15,933
وَطَفِقْتُ أَتَذَكَّرُ الْكَذِبَ وَأَقُولُ بِمَاذَا أَخْرُجُ مِنْ سَخَطِهِ غَدًا

270
00:20:16,316 --> 00:20:19,356
 وَاسْتَعَنْتُ عَلَى ذَلِكَ بِكُلِّ ذِي رَأْيٍ مِنْ أَهْلِي

271
00:20:19,717 --> 00:20:24,153
And then when I heard the news that Rasool Allah ﷺ is on his way back.

272
00:20:24,703 --> 00:20:27,533
I became very anxious.

273
00:20:28,045 --> 00:20:33,731
And then I was thinking about lying and trying to fabricate an excuse

274
00:20:34,017 --> 00:20:38,596
to get out of the anger of Rasool Allah ﷺ, when I meet him.

275
00:20:39,046 --> 00:20:44,787
And then he said, and I was seeking counsel, from all of those from my family,

276
00:20:45,229 --> 00:20:48,011
whom have an opinion that, I trust.

277
00:20:48,477 --> 00:20:53,476
فَلَمَّا قِيلَ إِنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَدْ أَظَلَّ قَادِمًا

278
00:20:53,918 --> 00:21:01,846
زَاحَ عَلَّيَّ الْبَاطِلُ وَعَرَفْتُ أَنِّي لَنْ أَخْرُجَ مِنْهُ أَبَدًا بِشَيْءٍ فِيهِ كَذِبٌ فَأَجْمَعْتُ صِدْقَهُ

279
00:21:02,608 --> 00:21:07,338
And then when I told that Rasool Allah ﷺ is almost here,

280
00:21:07,567 --> 00:21:11,368
all of the falsehood and those thoughts left my mind.

281
00:21:11,630 --> 00:21:16,665
And I knew that I'm not going to get out of this trouble at all, if I lie.

282
00:21:16,982 --> 00:21:19,543
And I decided that I'm going to speak the truth.

283
00:21:20,030 --> 00:21:24,454
And here you can see Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك), this righteous and great companion,

284
00:21:24,744 --> 00:21:28,973
falling into deep trouble and committing a serious mistake,

285
00:21:29,282 --> 00:21:35,285
but because of his Eeman(إيمان), and because of the Tarbiyyah(تربيعة) that his Eeman(إيمان) gave him,

286
00:21:35,595 --> 00:21:44,521
he was able to pull himself out of this hole that he made for himself through his good deeds.

287
00:21:45,126 --> 00:21:49,104
The decision that Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك) made to speak the truth and not to lie,

288
00:21:49,283 --> 00:21:54,966
as we will see is what saved him, from this big problem that he got himself into.

289
00:21:55,006 --> 00:21:59,400
I mean, you will see how serious staying behind is.?

290
00:22:00,076 --> 00:22:02,831
وَأَصْبَحَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَادِمًا

291
00:22:03,197 --> 00:22:09,968
وَكَانَ إِذَا قَدِمَ مِنْ سَفَرٍ بَدَأَ بِالْمَسْجِدِ فَيَرْكَعُ فِيهِ رَكْعَتَيْنِ ثُمَّ جَلَسَ لِلنَّاسِ

292
00:22:10,394 --> 00:22:15,098
Rasool Allah ﷺ arrived in the morning and when he would arrive from traveling

293
00:22:15,201 --> 00:22:18,364
he would first go to the Masjid(مسجد) and pray two Rak'ah(ركعة)

294
00:22:18,516 --> 00:22:21,680
and then Rasool Allah ﷺ sat down for the people

295
00:22:21,826 --> 00:22:24,745
because the people would come and meet Rasool Allah ﷺ.

296
00:22:24,770 --> 00:22:27,527
So he would sit in the Masjid(مسجد) and they would come and meet him in the Masjid(مسجد).

297
00:22:28,183 --> 00:22:30,855
That was the congregation place for the people, the Masjid(مسجد).

298
00:22:31,277 --> 00:22:37,395
فَلَمَّا فَعَلَ ذَلِكَ جَاءَهُ الْمُخَلَّفُونَ فَطَفِقُوا يَعْتَذِرُونَ إِلَيْهِ وَيَحْلِفُونَ لَهُ

299
00:22:37,859 --> 00:22:44,193
And when he did that, the ones who stayed behind came to Rasool Allah ﷺ giving their excuses

300
00:22:44,373 --> 00:22:49,157
and swearing, making an oath in the name of Allah that we're speaking the truth.

301
00:22:49,481 --> 00:22:51,546
وَكَانُوا بِضْعَةً وَثَمَانِينَ رَجُلًا

302
00:22:51,668 --> 00:22:53,561
And they were above 80 men.

303
00:22:54,214 --> 00:23:02,114
فَقَبِلَ مِنْهُمْ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ عَلَانِيَتَهُمْ وَبَايَعَهُمْ وَاسْتَغْفَرَ لَهُمْ وَوَكَلَ سَرَائِرَهُمْ إِلَى اللَّهِ

304
00:23:02,603 --> 00:23:05,936
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ accepted their excuses,

305
00:23:06,252 --> 00:23:10,808
and took what is apparent, took their words at face value.

306
00:23:11,296 --> 00:23:14,410
And he took their pledge of allegiance, their Bay'ayah(بيعه).

307
00:23:14,649 --> 00:23:20,330
And he asked Allah to forgive them and he left the insides of their hearts to Allah.

308
00:23:20,749 --> 00:23:26,269
And this is a general rule that Rasool Allah ﷺ applied that he would go by what is the apparent.

309
00:23:26,293 --> 00:23:27,170
اَلْاَخَذُ بِاالظَّاهِرْ

310
00:23:27,194 --> 00:23:30,396
And this is a very important rule that has a lot of implications.

311
00:23:30,936 --> 00:23:36,821
We judge people according to what we see, if we see Eeman(ايمان) outwardly,

312
00:23:37,078 --> 00:23:41,289
we judge that they are believers, even if they are disbelievers in their heart,

313
00:23:41,707 --> 00:23:45,499
if what we see from them, or acts of disbelief, Kuffr(كفر),

314
00:23:45,885 --> 00:23:51,508
then we judge them according to that even, if they are believers in their heart.

315
00:23:51,842 --> 00:23:52,747
That is the rule.

316
00:23:52,926 --> 00:23:56,343
And then we leave what is inside the hearts to Allah on the Day of Judgment.

317
00:23:56,613 --> 00:24:01,655
But the rules that apply in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا), apply to what is apparent and not what is hidden.

318
00:24:02,303 --> 00:24:04,759
And this is both for Islam(اسلام) and Kuffr(كفر).

319
00:24:05,200 --> 00:24:09,796
فَجِئْتُهُ فَلَمَّا سَلَّمْتُ عَلَيْهِ تَبَسَّمَ تَبَسُّمَ الْمُغْضَبِ

320
00:24:10,214 --> 00:24:18,262
ثُمَّ قَالَ تَعَالَى فَجِئْتُ أَمْشِي حَتَّى جَلَسْتُ بَيْنَ يَدَيْهِ فَقَالَ لِي مَا خَلَّفَكَ

321
00:24:18,916 --> 00:24:24,209
So, I came to Rasool Allah ﷺ and I gave him Salaam(سلام), and he smiled to me

322
00:24:24,463 --> 00:24:27,272
but it was a smile, of one, who was angry.

323
00:24:27,644 --> 00:24:30,549
And then he said: Come here, so I came walking to him.

324
00:24:30,850 --> 00:24:36,985
And then I sat in front of him and he asked me and said: Why did you stay behind?

325
00:24:37,799 --> 00:24:42,329
Rasool Allah ﷺ is asking Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك), Why did you stay behind?

326
00:24:42,989 --> 00:24:45,918
And we will be asked why did we stay behind?

327
00:24:46,406 --> 00:24:50,058
Not by Rasool Allah ﷺ, but by Allahعَزّ وجَلّ on the Day of Judgment.

328
00:24:50,506 --> 00:24:57,051
Rasool Allah ﷺ was there to ask Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك), and that question still holds true today.

329
00:24:57,314 --> 00:25:03,969
And it holds true in every time, when fighting Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(في سبيل الله) is a duty upon the Muslims.

330
00:25:04,238 --> 00:25:07,521
Why did you stay behind, what is your answer?

331
00:25:07,823 --> 00:25:09,801
Prepare an answer for Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

332
00:25:10,261 --> 00:25:11,988
Prepare an answer for this question.

333
00:25:12,225 --> 00:25:15,630
Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك) has thought about this question deeply.

334
00:25:15,781 --> 00:25:18,150
And he decided that he's going to speak the truth.

335
00:25:18,559 --> 00:25:19,973
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ told him.

336
00:25:20,005 --> 00:25:22,002
أَلَمْ تَكُنْ قَدْ ابْتَعْتَ ظَهْرَكَ

337
00:25:22,391 --> 00:25:24,496
Didn't you buy your mount?

338
00:25:24,852 --> 00:25:31,112
So, this shows us that Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك) was not completely ignoring his duty.

339
00:25:31,583 --> 00:25:37,262
He actually tried to prepare and he went as far as buying a mount.

340
00:25:37,789 --> 00:25:42,248
I mean, it's not like he was completely oblivious to the situation.

341
00:25:42,548 --> 00:25:46,594
No, he was thinking about it, and as we have seen, that he was so concerned

342
00:25:46,618 --> 00:25:50,272
and he would make the Niyyah(نية) everyday that he is going to get ready but he didn't.

343
00:25:50,963 --> 00:25:52,975
Rasool Allah ﷺ told him: Didn't to buy your mount?

344
00:25:53,015 --> 00:25:54,637
He said: Balaa(بلى), Yes.

345
00:25:54,915 --> 00:25:55,578
And then he said;

346
00:25:55,942 --> 00:25:59,597
 إِنِّي وَاللَّهِ لَوْ جَلَسْتُ عِنْدَ غَيْرِكَ مِنْ أَهْلِ الدُّنْيَا

347
00:25:59,723 --> 00:26:04,685
لَرَأَيْتُ أَنْ سَأَخْرُجُ مِنْ سَخَطِهِ بِعُذْرٍ وَلَقَدْ أُعْطِيتُ جَدَلًا

348
00:26:05,384 --> 00:26:11,632
He said: In the name of Allah, if I sat with someone else from the people of Duniyah(دُنِيَّا),

349
00:26:11,995 --> 00:26:20,380
I would have assumed that I will be able to get out of his anger with an excuse.

350
00:26:20,814 --> 00:26:22,635
وَلَقَدْ أُعْطِيتُ جَدَلًا

351
00:26:22,788 --> 00:26:29,540
He said: And I have the eloquence and I have the ability to argue.

352
00:26:30,241 --> 00:26:32,397
Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك) was a poet,

353
00:26:32,571 --> 00:26:37,695
and he was one of the famous and important poets of Madina,

354
00:26:37,931 --> 00:26:41,782
who defended Islam and Rasool Allah ﷺ with their poetry.

355
00:26:41,899 --> 00:26:44,581
I mean, the most famous poets of Madina were

356
00:26:44,621 --> 00:26:48,288
 Hassan Bin Thabit(حسان بن ثابت), Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك) and Abdullah Bin Rawaha(عبدالله بن رواحة).

357
00:26:48,352 --> 00:26:52,877
So, he was one of the three top poets of Rasool Allah صلوات الله وسلام عليه.

358
00:26:53,315 --> 00:26:54,116
So, he's saying;

359
00:26:54,156 --> 00:26:55,276
وَلَقَدْ أُعْطِيتُ جَدَلًا

360
00:26:55,480 --> 00:26:58,965
I have been gifted with the ability to debate and argue.

361
00:26:59,399 --> 00:27:03,929
I mean, he's a man who could convince you, with his point of view.

362
00:27:04,214 --> 00:27:05,584
In other words, he's saying;

363
00:27:05,873 --> 00:27:12,964
that I could, O Messenger of Allah, give excuses that will sound valid and convincing.

364
00:27:13,343 --> 00:27:21,439
But I realized that speaking this to you, would eventually be exposed because you are the Messenger of Allah,

365
00:27:22,015 --> 00:27:27,244
my lie will not go that far and I will be exposed.

366
00:27:27,888 --> 00:27:30,481
So, here, he's saying that I'm going to speak the truth.

367
00:27:31,126 --> 00:27:33,118
Now, with this statement of Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك),

368
00:27:33,406 --> 00:27:33,912
when he says;

369
00:27:33,952 --> 00:27:35,141
وَلَقَدْ أُعْطِيتُ جَدَلًا

370
00:27:35,426 --> 00:27:38,924
I have been given the ability to argue or convince.

371
00:27:39,530 --> 00:27:50,269
Nowadays, many arguments are made for excusing oneself, of fulfilling their duties towards Allah, and religion of Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

372
00:27:50,696 --> 00:27:54,599
And the most convincing arguments come from people who have a background in knowledge,

373
00:27:54,879 --> 00:27:57,468
the people who are well versed with the evidences,

374
00:27:57,508 --> 00:28:01,601
 so they have the ability to pull out some Ayaat(آيات) of Qur'an and to pull out some Ahadith(احاديث)

375
00:28:01,625 --> 00:28:05,740
and to pull out some statements and then bring them together in a way,

376
00:28:06,041 --> 00:28:11,931
that may sound convincing as presenting an argument that gives them an excuse.

377
00:28:12,209 --> 00:28:15,151
For example, you would have people say that we are in Makkah

378
00:28:15,561 --> 00:28:17,794
and you would have others say that we are in the weak stage.

379
00:28:17,819 --> 00:28:20,390
So, we need to apply the rules that apply to the weak stage.

380
00:28:20,726 --> 00:28:29,480
Now, the thing here is, yes, there was a situation once upon a time 1400 years ago, when Rasool Allah ﷺ was in Makkah,

381
00:28:29,823 --> 00:28:34,996
that they applied rules of weakness before they went to Madina.

382
00:28:35,368 --> 00:28:39,482
So, a person may come today and say that we are in Makkah.

383
00:28:39,580 --> 00:28:41,259
So, you go to that brother and tell him;

384
00:28:41,299 --> 00:28:45,637
Well fine, if you are in Makkah, then why don't you go to Madina,

385
00:28:46,219 --> 00:28:51,107
Rasool Allah ﷺ when he was in Makkah, he struggled to go to Madina.

386
00:28:51,521 --> 00:28:58,335
So, if you are now in Makkah stage, why don't you struggle to go to the Madina stage.

387
00:28:58,800 --> 00:29:00,678
The thing is that, he wouldn't want to.

388
00:29:00,773 --> 00:29:01,526
Why?

389
00:29:01,649 --> 00:29:04,860
Because the pay in Madina is less than the pay in Makkah.

390
00:29:05,346 --> 00:29:10,430
The life in Makkah is more comfortable than it is going to be in Madina.

391
00:29:10,731 --> 00:29:14,226
And therefore this person is not willing to make the move.

392
00:29:15,034 --> 00:29:17,938
The person would say that we are in the stage of weakness,

393
00:29:18,153 --> 00:29:22,533
well fine, if you're in the stage of weakness, then prepare yourself to get out of it.

394
00:29:23,029 --> 00:29:28,711
But the thing is, you would find that person unwilling to prepare to get out of it,

395
00:29:28,910 --> 00:29:37,107
because he knows very well that the path to strength is a path that is paved with difficulty and sacrifice.

396
00:29:37,588 --> 00:29:42,978
Rasool Allah ﷺ, Yes at one point of time, he was in Makkah and the Muslims were in Makkah,

397
00:29:43,379 --> 00:29:49,978
but they did all, what was humanly capable for them to do in order to get out of that situation.

398
00:29:50,252 --> 00:29:54,122
If you look at the Seerah(سيرة) of Rasool Allah ﷺ you see that it is fascinating.

399
00:29:54,431 --> 00:30:00,897
How Rasool Allah ﷺ would knock on every door possible to find a way out of Makkah.

400
00:30:00,921 --> 00:30:05,064
I mean, Rasool Allah ﷺ would meet with the tribes, in every season of Hajj(حج),

401
00:30:05,377 --> 00:30:09,406
asking them to give him support, so that he can make Hijrah(هجرة) to them.

402
00:30:09,979 --> 00:30:12,625
And when you do something once and twice and three times

403
00:30:12,649 --> 00:30:16,985
and everytime you get the same answer of rejection, you end up giving up.

404
00:30:17,274 --> 00:30:21,446
Rasool Allah ﷺ, never gave up and he would do that year in and year out.

405
00:30:21,591 --> 00:30:27,161
And he will do that with first tribe, second tribe, third tribe, fourth tribe, fifth tribe and never give up

406
00:30:27,479 --> 00:30:30,432
 until, eventually he met with Al-Ansaar(أنْصَار),

407
00:30:30,569 --> 00:30:34,141
and they are the ones who provided him with a base to spread the Daw'ah(دعوة) .

408
00:30:34,356 --> 00:30:40,770
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ was trying every avenue possible to get out of Makkah and go to Madina.

409
00:30:41,126 --> 00:30:46,905
He tried every avenue possible to get out of the stage of weakness into the stage of strength.

410
00:30:47,092 --> 00:30:52,879
So, whoever today is saying that we are in Makkah, that person needs to get out of Makkah,

411
00:30:53,289 --> 00:30:58,874
and whoever is in a state of weakness needs to struggle to get out of that state of weakness.

412
00:30:59,111 --> 00:31:03,918
Otherwise, the Ayah(آية) of Allahعَزّوجَلّ that applies, would apply to them.

413
00:31:04,266 --> 00:31:05,462
Where Allahعَزّوجَلّ saysl;

414
00:31:05,661 --> 00:31:07,972
وَلَوْ أَرَادُوا الْخُرُوجَ لَأَعَدُّوا لَهُ عُدَّةً

415
00:31:08,062 --> 00:31:10,960
If they want to go out, they would have prepared to do so.

416
00:31:11,719 --> 00:31:13,274
But without any preparation.

417
00:31:13,372 --> 00:31:17,515
That means that the person is just paying lip service and it is not true.

418
00:31:18,059 --> 00:31:24,408
So, Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك) is saying that I'm not going to use my argumentative abilities and debating abilities here.

419
00:31:24,805 --> 00:31:25,375
He said;

420
00:31:25,780 --> 00:31:32,696
وَلَئِنْ حَدَّثْتُكَ حَدِيثَ صِدْقٍ تَجِدُ عَلَيَّ فِيهِ إِنِّي لَأَرْجُو فِيهِ عَفْوَ اللَّهِ

421
00:31:33,087 --> 00:31:37,875
He said: And if I speak the truth to you, even though it might make you angry,

422
00:31:38,262 --> 00:31:44,284
but I am expecting that in the truth, will be the forgiveness of Allah.

423
00:31:44,835 --> 00:31:47,326
لَا وَاللَّهِ مَا كَانَ لِي مِنْ عُذْرٍ

424
00:31:47,650 --> 00:31:49,612
I have no excuse.

425
00:31:50,072 --> 00:31:55,232
He made it clear to Rasool Allah ﷺ that he has no excuse in staying behind.

426
00:31:56,155 --> 00:32:01,142
وَاللَّهِ مَا كُنْتُ قَطُّ أَقْوَى وَلَا أَيْسَرَ مِنِّي حِينَ تَخَلَّفْتُ عَنْكَ

427
00:32:01,166 --> 00:32:05,730
I was never stronger and more able to go out when I stayed behind.

428
00:32:06,104 --> 00:32:11,528
فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَمَّا هَذَا فَقَدْ صَدَقَ فَقُمْ حَتَّى يَقْضِيَ اللَّهُ فِيكَ

429
00:32:12,196 --> 00:32:14,971
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: This man has spoken the truth,

430
00:32:15,327 --> 00:32:19,587
so leave until Allah judges in your situation.

431
00:32:20,048 --> 00:32:28,128
فَقُمْتُ وَثَارَ رِجَالٌ مِنْ بَنِي سَلِمَةَ فَاتَّبَعُونِي فَقَالُوا لِي وَاللَّهِ مَا عَلِمْنَاكَ كُنْتَ أَذْنَبْتَ ذَنْبًا قَبْلَ هَذَا

432
00:32:28,554 --> 00:32:35,885
وَلَقَدْ عَجَزْتَ أَنْ لَا تَكُونَ اعْتَذَرْتَ إِلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بِمَا اعْتَذَرَ إِلَيْهِ الْمُتَخَلِّفُونَ

433
00:32:36,382 --> 00:32:41,838
قَدْ كَانَ كَافِيَكَ ذَنْبَكَ اسْتِغْفَارُ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ لَكَ

434
00:32:42,124 --> 00:32:47,616
فَوَاللَّهِ مَا زَالُوا يُؤَنِّبُونِي حَتَّى أَرَدْتُ أَنْ أَرْجِعَ فَأُكَذِّبَ نَفْسِي

435
00:32:47,888 --> 00:32:54,612
He said: So I left and some men from my clan followed me and they told me;

436
00:32:54,883 --> 00:33:00,433
We never know that you have committed a sin before this, this is the first time.

437
00:33:01,024 --> 00:33:06,312
Why didn't you give an excuse to Rasool Allah ﷺ just like everybody else did

438
00:33:06,769 --> 00:33:10,587
and it would have been sufficient for you, the Istaghfaar(إستغفار) of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

439
00:33:10,611 --> 00:33:13,705
Because the ones, who came before Rasool Allah ﷺ ask Allah to forgive them.

440
00:33:13,784 --> 00:33:17,513
So, they told him: If you have came up with an excuse,

441
00:33:17,538 --> 00:33:24,134
Rasool Allah ﷺ would ask Allah for your forgiveness, and that would be sufficient enough to wipe out your sin.

442
00:33:24,297 --> 00:33:30,827
And he said: And they were blaming me, until I thought about going back to Rasool Allah ﷺ, and making up an excuse.

443
00:33:31,199 --> 00:33:32,077
 But then I asked them.

444
00:33:32,101 --> 00:33:35,202
ثُمَّ قُلْتُ لَهُمْ هَلْ لَقِيَ هَذَا مَعِي أَحَدٌ

445
00:33:35,480 --> 00:33:38,875
Did anybody else say the same thing and get the same response.

446
00:33:38,906 --> 00:33:41,861
قَالُوا نَعَمْ رَجُلَانِ قَالَا مِثْلَ مَا قُلْتَ

447
00:33:41,885 --> 00:33:43,282
They said: Yes, Two men.

448
00:33:43,497 --> 00:33:45,694
They said: Like what you have said.

449
00:33:45,729 --> 00:33:48,598
فَقِيلَ لَهُمَا مِثْلُ مَا قِيلَ لَكَ

450
00:33:48,875 --> 00:33:52,417
And they were told similar answer to what was told to you.

451
00:33:52,451 --> 00:33:53,335
فَقُلْتُ مَنْ هُمَا

452
00:33:53,359 --> 00:33:54,088
I said: Who are they?

453
00:33:54,310 --> 00:33:58,927
قَالُوا مُرَارَةُ بْنُ الرَّبِيعِ الْعَمْرِيُّ وَهِلَالُ بْنُ أُمَيَّةَ الْوَاقِفِيُّ

454
00:33:59,423 --> 00:34:01,669
They said: Mirarah(مرارة) and Hillal(هلال).

455
00:34:01,860 --> 00:34:05,991
فَذَكَرُوا لِي رَجُلَيْنِ صَالِحَيْنِ قَدْ شَهِدَا بَدْرًا فِيهِمَا أُسْوَةٌ

456
00:34:06,175 --> 00:34:08,353
They mentioned to me two righteous men.

457
00:34:08,883 --> 00:34:14,816
And I saw them as examples for me or these were two men.

458
00:34:14,841 --> 00:34:18,186
So, therefore there's somebody else who did the same thing that I have did,

459
00:34:18,210 --> 00:34:20,211
and therefore he decided that he's not going to go back.

460
00:34:21,059 --> 00:34:26,955
And this shows you that, we find when we will see company that gives us support.

461
00:34:27,810 --> 00:34:36,126
So, when he saw that he has company in the action that he did, in telling the truth that encouraged him to carry on.

462
00:34:36,407 --> 00:34:40,301
And this shows us the importance of having good company around you.

463
00:34:40,640 --> 00:34:45,175
Because of the pressure of the society, see he was pressured to go back and make up a lie.

464
00:34:45,486 --> 00:34:46,714
And he was almost going to do that.

465
00:34:46,960 --> 00:34:48,894
So, the pressure of the society is very strong.

466
00:34:48,918 --> 00:34:53,481
And therefore you need to surround yourself with like minded people,

467
00:34:53,505 --> 00:34:58,945
who will support you to do good, especially for those who are living in rotten environments,

468
00:34:59,316 --> 00:35:03,340
in environments that are environments of disbelief and environments of Fitnah(فِتْنَه).

469
00:35:03,798 --> 00:35:08,137
It's very important that you don't trust your abilities in survival,

470
00:35:08,399 --> 00:35:10,799
and you realize that you are weak human being.

471
00:35:11,130 --> 00:35:12,453
خُلِقَ الْإِنْسَانُ ضَعِيفًا

472
00:35:12,722 --> 00:35:16,525
A man has been created in a weak state, we are weak.

473
00:35:16,746 --> 00:35:21,741
And therefore we need to have good company, it's very important to have likeminded people

474
00:35:22,053 --> 00:35:24,958
who would support you and advise you and Deenan Naseeha( دين النصيحه).

475
00:35:24,999 --> 00:35:27,442
Rasool Allah ﷺ says, that Religion is advice.

476
00:35:27,678 --> 00:35:31,663
So, you need to have people around you, who would encourage you to do good.

477
00:35:31,909 --> 00:35:37,680
I would strongly advise anybody who is not in such an environment to change their environment immediately.

478
00:35:37,912 --> 00:35:43,679
Because if you are strong today, you might become vulnerable and weak tomorrow.

479
00:35:43,962 --> 00:35:47,118
And you never know how deep you would fall.

480
00:35:47,818 --> 00:35:52,604
And in a time like this, there's no end to how low a person could get.

481
00:35:52,628 --> 00:35:56,711
I mean, some people can keep on descending and descending and descending,

482
00:35:56,942 --> 00:36:00,590
getting deeper and deeperand deeper until, they become a disbeliever

483
00:36:00,614 --> 00:36:02,237
until, they become Murtadd(مرتد).

484
00:36:02,555 --> 00:36:04,429
So, it's very dangerous thing.

485
00:36:04,587 --> 00:36:08,689
Don't underestimate the effect of your environment on you.

486
00:36:09,272 --> 00:36:11,184
فَمَضَيْتُ حِينَ ذَكَرُوهُمَا لِي

487
00:36:11,532 --> 00:36:17,106
 وَنَهَى رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ الْمُسْلِمِينَ عَنْ كَلَامِنَا أَيُّهَا الثَّلَاثَةُ مِنْ بَيْنِ مَنْ تَخَلَّفَ عَنْهُ

488
00:36:17,478 --> 00:36:20,787
Out of all of the people who stayed behind, and remember that, they were over 80,

489
00:36:21,268 --> 00:36:26,657
the three of us, Rasool Allah ﷺ has given orders that we should be boycotted

490
00:36:27,043 --> 00:36:30,795
in terms of speaking, it's not an economical boycott against them.

491
00:36:30,820 --> 00:36:35,199
It is a boycott of not speaking to them, not interacting with them.

492
00:36:35,789 --> 00:36:39,629
So, Subhaan Allah(سبحان الله), the ones who spoke the truth, end up getting boycotted,

493
00:36:40,016 --> 00:36:46,427
while the ones, who lied, their excuse was accepted and they're fine.

494
00:36:46,997 --> 00:36:50,807
But you will see that this is only a short term thing and it's short lived.

495
00:36:51,194 --> 00:36:57,688
And this is a test from Allahعَزّوجَلّ, sometimes a lie gives you an instant gratification

496
00:36:57,712 --> 00:37:02,402
and gives you an instant, very short lived solution.

497
00:37:02,726 --> 00:37:05,911
But after that things began to unravel.

498
00:37:06,251 --> 00:37:09,487
While truth in the long term is always good.

499
00:37:10,632 --> 00:37:18,269
فَاجْتَنَبَنَا النَّاسُ وَتَغَيَّرُوا لَنَا حَتَّى تَنَكَّرَتْ فِي نَفْسِي الْأَرْضُ فَمَا هِيَ الَّتِي أَعْرِفُ

500
00:37:18,605 --> 00:37:24,887
He said: People boycotted us, stayed away from us and their treatment changed.

501
00:37:25,556 --> 00:37:27,760
He said: It was so bad,

502
00:37:27,943 --> 00:37:30,091
حَتَّى تَنَكَّرَتْ فِي نَفْسِي الْأَرْضُ

503
00:37:30,353 --> 00:37:33,910
Until the land has become like unknown to me.

504
00:37:34,211 --> 00:37:36,225
I mean, it's not, Subhaan Allah(سبحان الله)

505
00:37:36,446 --> 00:37:38,802
He's in Madina, he is from Madina.

506
00:37:38,986 --> 00:37:43,001
That's his home, he lived there all of his life, that's where he was born.

507
00:37:43,526 --> 00:37:49,146
But because the people changed, he even felt that the ground, he's standing upon is different.

508
00:37:49,611 --> 00:37:51,622
It's like an unknown land to him.

509
00:37:51,906 --> 00:37:57,081
You feel homesick in your own home, you feel like a foreigner in your own land.

510
00:37:57,742 --> 00:38:02,376
Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك) is saying that even the land was different to me.

511
00:38:02,716 --> 00:38:05,798
Why? Because the people are boycotting him.

512
00:38:06,654 --> 00:38:09,132
فَلَبِثْنَا عَلَى ذَلِكَ خَمْسِينَ لَيْلَةً

513
00:38:09,164 --> 00:38:11,145
That carried on for 50 days.

514
00:38:11,474 --> 00:38:15,837
فَأَمَّا صَاحِبَايَ فَاسْتَكَانَا وَقَعَدَا فِي بُيُوتِهِمَا يَبْكِيَانِ

515
00:38:16,068 --> 00:38:20,859
He said: My two companions, they just gave up and sat at home weeping.

516
00:38:21,289 --> 00:38:24,734
وَأَمَّا أَنَا فَكُنْتُ أَشَبَّ الْقَوْمِ وَأَجْلَدَهُمْ

517
00:38:24,918 --> 00:38:30,281
 فَكُنْتُ أَخْرُجُ فَأَشْهَدُ الصَّلَاةَ مَعَ الْمُسْلِمِينَ وَأَطُوفُ فِي الْأَسْوَاقِ وَلَا يُكَلِّمُنِي أَحَدٌ

518
00:38:30,668 --> 00:38:34,173
He said: But me, I was the youngest among them, and the toughest.

519
00:38:34,435 --> 00:38:38,414
So, I would go out and I would pray in Jama'ah(جماعة) and I would go in the markets,

520
00:38:38,637 --> 00:38:40,245
but nobody would speak to me.

521
00:38:40,372 --> 00:38:46,794
So, the other two, they just gave up, they couldn't handle walking around with people ignoring them.

522
00:38:47,009 --> 00:38:50,510
And they just sat at home and they were crying, devastated.

523
00:38:50,763 --> 00:38:55,766
But Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك) he was strong, so he would go out and pray Jama'ah(جماعة)

524
00:38:56,236 --> 00:39:00,487
and go in the market, even though he would be completely ignored.

525
00:39:00,760 --> 00:39:05,036
And this also shows us how strong, the society, the community was.

526
00:39:05,061 --> 00:39:08,361
I mean, an order from Rasool Allah ﷺ to boycott them, that's it, it was final.

527
00:39:08,623 --> 00:39:12,667
Nobody would speak, you go to the marketplace nobody is speaking,

528
00:39:12,691 --> 00:39:16,642
go to the Masjid(مسجد) nobody speaking, total obedience to Rasool Allah ﷺ.

529
00:39:17,474 --> 00:39:20,560
And this is why Hajar(هجر) was powerful, boycotting was powerful

530
00:39:21,127 --> 00:39:26,330
because the whole society takes the command from Rasool Allah ﷺ and do what they're told.

531
00:39:26,864 --> 00:39:31,717
وَآتِي رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَأُسَلِّمُ عَلَيْهِ وَهُوَ فِي مَجْلِسِهِ بَعْدَ الصَّلَاةِ

532
00:39:31,742 --> 00:39:34,856
فَأَقُولُ فِي نَفْسِي هَلْ حَرَّكَ شَفَتَيْهِ بِرَدِّ السَّلَامِ عَلَيَّ أَمْ لَا

533
00:39:35,174 --> 00:39:38,082
And I would go to Rasool Allah ﷺ, when he was in his gathering

534
00:39:38,401 --> 00:39:39,885
and I would give him salam(سلام)

535
00:39:40,385 --> 00:39:46,858
and I would ask myself did he move his lips in responding to my Salam(سلام).

536
00:39:47,493 --> 00:39:49,546
 So, Rasool Allah ﷺ would not answer him,

537
00:39:49,859 --> 00:39:54,618
so he'd tried to stare at the lips and see if Rasool Allah ﷺ is doing it quietly.

538
00:39:55,144 --> 00:40:03,636
ثُمَّ أُصَلِّي قَرِيبًا مِنْهُ فَأُسَارِقُهُ النَّظَرَ فَإِذَا أَقْبَلْتُ عَلَى صَلَاتِي أَقْبَلَ إِلَيَّ وَإِذَا الْتَفَتُّ نَحْوَهُ أَعْرَضَ عَنِّي

539
00:40:03,899 --> 00:40:06,460
And when I would be Salah(صلاة), I would look at him

540
00:40:07,058 --> 00:40:13,836
and when I would be concentrating on my Salah(صلاة) and looking down, Rasool Allah ﷺ would stare at me

541
00:40:14,104 --> 00:40:20,058
and when I would, then move my eyes towards him and look at him, Rasool Allah ﷺ would turn away.

542
00:40:20,613 --> 00:40:22,176
So, Rasool Ullah would only look at him

543
00:40:22,490 --> 00:40:27,129
when Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك) was not looking at the Rasool Allah ﷺ.

544
00:40:27,641 --> 00:40:34,989
حَتَّى إِذَا طَالَ عَلَيَّ ذَلِكَ مِنْ جَفْوَةِ النَّاسِ مَشَيْتُ حَتَّى تَسَوَّرْتُ جِدَارَ حَائِطِ أَبِي قَتَادَةَ

545
00:40:35,376 --> 00:40:40,641
وَهُوَ ابْنُ عَمِّي وَأَحَبُّ النَّاسِ إِلَيَّ فَسَلَّمْتُ عَلَيْهِ فَوَاللَّهِ مَا رَدَّ عَلَيَّ السَّلَامَ

546
00:40:41,247 --> 00:40:45,176
And when this has extended and became so long,

547
00:40:45,691 --> 00:40:52,340
I went and climbed the wall of the house of Abu Qatadah(ابو قتاده), who was my cousin

548
00:40:52,597 --> 00:40:54,967
and the most beloved person to me,

549
00:40:55,190 --> 00:40:58,804
so I gave him Salam(سلام) and he didn't even respond back.

550
00:40:59,340 --> 00:41:02,718
فَقُلْتُ يَا أَبَا قَتَادَةَ أَنْشُدُكَ بِاللَّهِ

551
00:41:03,162 --> 00:41:10,405
 هَلْ تَعْلَمُنِي أُحِبُّ اللَّهَ وَرَسُولَهُ فَسَكَتَ فَعُدْتُ لَهُ فَنَشَدْتُهُ فَسَكَتَ

552
00:41:11,123 --> 00:41:15,464
فَعُدْتُ لَهُ فَنَشَدْتُهُ فَقَالَ اللَّهُ وَرَسُولُهُ أَعْلَمُ

553
00:41:15,948 --> 00:41:19,964
 فَفَاضَتْ عَيْنَايَ وَتَوَلَّيْتُ حَتَّى تَسَوَّرْتُ الْجِدَارَ

554
00:41:20,238 --> 00:41:23,066
I said: O Abu Qatadah(ابو قتاده)! I ask you in the name of Allah.

555
00:41:23,414 --> 00:41:27,189
Do you know me, to be a person who loves Allah and His Messenger?

556
00:41:27,576 --> 00:41:28,766
So, he was silent.

557
00:41:28,989 --> 00:41:30,819
I asked him again, he was silent.

558
00:41:30,859 --> 00:41:33,192
I Ask him again, he was silent.

559
00:41:33,559 --> 00:41:36,996
And then, I asked him and he said: Allah and His Messenger know best.

560
00:41:37,174 --> 00:41:40,901
So, my eyes were swelling with tears, and I walked out.

561
00:41:41,797 --> 00:41:44,323
And even his cousin wouldn't speak to him.

562
00:41:44,810 --> 00:41:48,018
قَالَ فَبَيْنَا أَنَا أَمْشِي بِسُوقِ الْمَدِينَةِ

563
00:41:48,359 --> 00:41:55,696
 إِذَا نَبَطِيٌّ مِنْ أَنْبَاطِ أَهْلِ الشَّأْمِ مِمَّنْ قَدِمَ بِالطَّعَامِ يَبِيعُهُ بِالْمَدِينَةِ

564
00:41:55,904 --> 00:42:03,973
يَقُولُ مَنْ يَدُلُّ عَلَى كَعْبِ بْنِ مَالِكٍ فَطَفِقَ النَّاسُ يُشِيرُونَ لَهُ حَتَّى إِذَا جَاءَنِي دَفَعَ إِلَيَّ كِتَابًا مِنْ مَلِكِ غَسَّانَ

565
00:42:04,570 --> 00:42:09,505
He said: While I was walking around in the market place of Madina.

566
00:42:09,977 --> 00:42:14,046
A Nabati(نبتي), the people of Nabatah(نبته) are from Jordan, in Ash-Shaam(الشام)

567
00:42:14,371 --> 00:42:19,344
and he was a merchant, who had some food to sell in Madina.

568
00:42:19,640 --> 00:42:23,268
He was asking the people to point out to him, Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك).

569
00:42:23,671 --> 00:42:25,982
So, they guided him towards me.

570
00:42:26,237 --> 00:42:31,063
And then he came to me and handed me a letter from the king of Ghassaan(غسان).

571
00:42:31,309 --> 00:42:35,935
The kingdom of Ghassaan(غسان) is a Christian, who hated the Muslims and hated the Rasool Allah ﷺ.

572
00:42:36,385 --> 00:42:40,614
It says in the books of Seerah(سيرة) that he wanted to draw an army

573
00:42:41,048 --> 00:42:47,019
and ask Heraculus for support, because he was a proxy of Heracul(هراقل).

574
00:42:47,044 --> 00:42:53,799
I mean, these were kings, who have had big titles and names but they were traitors and agents for Heracul(هراقل).

575
00:42:54,403 --> 00:42:58,036
So, he wanted to ask permission from Heracul(هراقل) to attack Madina.

576
00:42:58,188 --> 00:43:05,615
It was actually Heracul(هراقل), who told him to stop and hold tight and not to attack Muhammadﷺ

577
00:43:05,655 --> 00:43:10,311
because Heracul(هراقل) knew that Muhammadﷺ was the Messenger of Allah.

578
00:43:10,424 --> 00:43:13,624
And he didn't want to start the confrontation with him.

579
00:43:13,886 --> 00:43:17,342
So, Subhaan Allah(سبحان الله), Heracul(هراقل) was wiser than the king of Ghassaan(غسان),

580
00:43:17,561 --> 00:43:21,947
who's an Arab and should have some sympathy towards Muhammadﷺ

581
00:43:22,241 --> 00:43:27,369
but it shows you how the traitors sometimes are worse than their masters.

582
00:43:27,809 --> 00:43:32,157
The King of Ghassaan(غسان) sent a letter to Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك).

583
00:43:32,182 --> 00:43:37,172
So this shows you that there were some information gathering going on

584
00:43:37,212 --> 00:43:39,952
 and there was interest, with what was happening in Madina.

585
00:43:40,311 --> 00:43:46,537
And the King of Ghassaan(غسان) caught word about what happened with Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك)

586
00:43:46,579 --> 00:43:47,846
and he sent him this letter.

587
00:43:48,064 --> 00:43:53,813
فَإِذَا فِيهِ أَمَّا بَعْدُ فَإِنَّهُ قَدْ بَلَغَنِي أَنَّ صَاحِبَكَ قَدْ جَفَاكَ

588
00:43:54,468 --> 00:43:59,458
وَلَمْ يَجْعَلْكَ اللَّهُ بِدَارِ هَوَانٍ وَلَا مَضْيَعَةٍ فَالْحَقْ بِنَا نُوَاسِكَ

589
00:43:59,911 --> 00:44:07,214
The letter stated that, I have heard that your friend has forsaken you, meaning Muhammadﷺ.

590
00:44:07,688 --> 00:44:16,825
And Allah, has not left you in a place where you would be humiliated and where you will be forsaken.

591
00:44:17,015 --> 00:44:20,214
 So, come to us, and we will take care of you.

592
00:44:20,835 --> 00:44:25,838
And here brothers and sisters, you see a characteristic of the Kuffar(كفار).

593
00:44:26,025 --> 00:44:33,824
The Kuffar(كفار) are going to try to draw in and strike deals with the Muslim leaders

594
00:44:33,919 --> 00:44:46,049
whom they see, as willing, or in a situation, where they agree with the Kuffar(كفار) on certain issues,

595
00:44:46,333 --> 00:44:51,919
it would show you that they will try to break in the Muslim ranks.

596
00:44:52,486 --> 00:44:59,550
Here, they're trying to draw out one of the prominent members of the Muslim community.

597
00:44:59,807 --> 00:45:04,592
They're trying to bring him in, not because they love him, not because they like him,

598
00:45:04,830 --> 00:45:07,651
but because they have an agenda.

599
00:45:07,963 --> 00:45:13,745
The King of Ghassaan(غسان) because of his hatred against Rasool Allah ﷺ and the Muslims.

600
00:45:14,056 --> 00:45:21,150
That is why.? He wants to infiltrate the Muslim society and pull out of it, Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك).

601
00:45:21,317 --> 00:45:23,932
This is something that they are doing today.

602
00:45:24,585 --> 00:45:28,966
They are willing to fund and pump money and just pour it,

603
00:45:29,361 --> 00:45:32,482
on any Muslims who are going to be sympathetic to their cause.

604
00:45:33,017 --> 00:45:40,702
They are willing to sit behind the scenes with Muslims who are willing to promote a watered down version of Islam,

605
00:45:41,153 --> 00:45:47,689
they are willing to sit and put hand in hand with the rand Muslims,

606
00:45:47,990 --> 00:45:53,641
who are willing to spread the version of Islam that is appealing to them.

607
00:45:54,458 --> 00:46:00,230
And they are willing to spend millions and millions of dollars for that.

608
00:46:00,597 --> 00:46:05,760
And Shaytan(شيطان) can come to some people and say, well, let's take that money

609
00:46:06,084 --> 00:46:08,114
and benefit the Daw'ah(دعوة) with it.

610
00:46:08,265 --> 00:46:09,501
Let's take that money

611
00:46:09,708 --> 00:46:15,006
and use it to build Masajid(مساجد) or to build schools or to do this or to do that.

612
00:46:15,268 --> 00:46:17,701
And all of that is deception of Shaytan(شيطان) because

613
00:46:17,726 --> 00:46:20,106
they are not going to give anything for free.

614
00:46:20,445 --> 00:46:24,820
They are going to take in exchange of what they give,

615
00:46:24,987 --> 00:46:27,427
they will definitely take from you something.

616
00:46:27,936 --> 00:46:30,928
So, how did Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك) respond,

617
00:46:31,213 --> 00:46:33,693
so that we can learn, how to respond?

618
00:46:33,924 --> 00:46:35,304
Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك) said;

619
00:46:35,569 --> 00:46:40,479
فَقُلْتُ لَمَّا قَرَأْتُهَا وَهَذَا أَيْضًا مِنْ الْبَلَاءِ

620
00:46:40,671 --> 00:46:43,899
When I read this, I said this is a trial from Allah.

621
00:46:44,066 --> 00:46:47,713
فَتَيَمَّمْتُ بِهَا التَّنُّورَ فَسَجَرْتُهُ بِهَا

622
00:46:47,761 --> 00:46:49,928
I took it and threw it in the fire.

623
00:46:50,390 --> 00:46:53,592
That's how we should deal with their deals.

624
00:46:53,774 --> 00:46:56,812
Take that deal and throw it in the fire

625
00:46:56,932 --> 00:46:59,599
and don't let such things stay behind.

626
00:46:59,639 --> 00:47:03,334
I mean, Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك) could have kept this letter as a souvenir.

627
00:47:03,696 --> 00:47:07,759
But he didn't he throw it in the fire because it's something dangerous.

628
00:47:08,075 --> 00:47:12,774
It's something that has a temptation in it. So, get rid of it.

629
00:47:13,107 --> 00:47:16,682
Don't let it sit behind, just throw it in the fire.

630
00:47:17,131 --> 00:47:20,279
حَتَّى إِذَا مَضَتْ أَرْبَعُونَ لَيْلَةً مِنْ الْخَمْسِينَ

631
00:47:20,529 --> 00:47:23,541
إِذَا رَسُولُ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَأْتِينِي

632
00:47:23,848 --> 00:47:30,209
فَقَالَ إِنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَأْمُرُكَ أَنْ تَعْتَزِلَ امْرَأَتَكَ

633
00:47:30,646 --> 00:47:35,767
فَقُلْتُ أُطَلِّقُهَا أَمْ مَاذَا أَفْعَلُ قَالَ لَا بَلْ اعْتَزِلْهَا وَلَا تَقْرَبْهَا

634
00:47:35,968 --> 00:47:40,857
 وَأَرْسَلَ إِلَى صَاحِبَيَّ مِثْلَ ذَلِكَ فَقُلْتُ لِامْرَأَتِي الْحَقِي بِأَهْلِكِ

635
00:47:41,131 --> 00:47:44,171
فَتَكُونِي عِنْدَهُمْ حَتَّى يَقْضِيَ اللَّهُ فِي هَذَا الْأَمْرِ

636
00:47:44,662 --> 00:47:49,131
Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك) said: A Messenger from Rasool Allah ﷺ came to me

637
00:47:49,541 --> 00:47:53,101
and said and this is after 40 days of the boycott.

638
00:47:53,496 --> 00:47:59,001
This Messenger came to me and said that Rasool Allah ﷺ is ordering you to leave your wife.

639
00:47:59,025 --> 00:48:01,530
He said: Shall I divorce her? He said: No.

640
00:48:01,712 --> 00:48:04,697
But stay away from her, meaning he cannot touch her.

641
00:48:04,987 --> 00:48:08,953
And he sent the same message to my other two companions.

642
00:48:09,269 --> 00:48:12,529
So, I told my wife go and stay with your family,

643
00:48:13,112 --> 00:48:17,289
go and stay with your parents, until Allah judges in this affair.

644
00:48:17,699 --> 00:48:23,266
قَالَ كَعْبٌ فَجَاءَتْ امْرَأَةُ هِلَالِ بْنِ أُمَيَّةَ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ

645
00:48:23,570 --> 00:48:28,538
فَقَالَتْ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ إِنَّ هِلَالَ بْنَ أُمَيَّةَ شَيْخٌ ضَائِعٌ

646
00:48:28,751 --> 00:48:35,390
لَيْسَ لَهُ خَادِمٌ فَهَلْ تَكْرَهُ أَنْ أَخْدُمَهُ قَالَ لَا وَلَكِنْ لَا يَقْرَبْكِ

647
00:48:35,501 --> 00:48:38,016
قَالَتْ إِنَّهُ وَاللَّهِ مَا بِهِ حَرَكَةٌ إِلَى شَيْءٍ

648
00:48:38,082 --> 00:48:42,323
وَاللَّهِ مَا زَالَ يَبْكِي مُنْذُ كَانَ مِنْ أَمْرِهِ مَا كَانَ إِلَى يَوْمِهِ هَذَا

649
00:48:42,858 --> 00:48:48,190
Ka'ab(كعب) said: The wife of Hilal Ibn Ummayyah(هلال ابن امية), one of the three came to Rasool Allah ﷺ and said;

650
00:48:48,230 --> 00:48:52,688
O Messenger of Allah Hilal Ibn Ummayyah(هلال ابن امية) is a lost old man.

651
00:48:53,173 --> 00:48:54,573
What does this strike you?

652
00:48:54,740 --> 00:48:58,256
Hilal Ibn Ummayyah(هلال ابن اميه) is an old man, who's lost.

653
00:48:58,485 --> 00:48:59,846
Does that strike you at all?

654
00:49:00,127 --> 00:49:01,168
What are we talking about here?

655
00:49:01,221 --> 00:49:03,222
We're talking about here, people who stayed behind from, what?

656
00:49:03,716 --> 00:49:08,710
These are people who stayed behind from fighting, actual war, battle.

657
00:49:09,199 --> 00:49:13,856
And she says that my husband is an old man, who's lost.

658
00:49:14,298 --> 00:49:18,231
So, Subhaan Allah(سبحان الله) here you have an old man, who's lost

659
00:49:18,604 --> 00:49:24,744
and nevertheless, Rasool Allah ﷺ boycotted him and ordered the Muslims to boycott him.

660
00:49:25,118 --> 00:49:29,168
Because Rasool Allah ﷺ considered that this man does not have an excuse.

661
00:49:29,304 --> 00:49:34,395
So, what excuse do the young fit, able, men have.

662
00:49:34,737 --> 00:49:37,499
If Hilal Ibn Ummayyah(هلال ابن امية) was not excused.

663
00:49:37,753 --> 00:49:39,864
What excuse does anybody else have?

664
00:49:40,505 --> 00:49:45,701
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ was asked by this woman, she said: He's a lost old man.

665
00:49:46,063 --> 00:49:48,659
Would you allow me to serve him?

666
00:49:48,905 --> 00:49:51,127
He said: No, but don't let him touch you.

667
00:49:51,267 --> 00:49:52,496
Meaning he cannot sleep with you.

668
00:49:52,707 --> 00:49:57,676
She said: In the name of Allah, he has no desire for anything.

669
00:49:58,196 --> 00:50:05,134
Since this issue began, he's been weeping until, this moment, until this day has been crying.

670
00:50:05,166 --> 00:50:07,113
He's not thinking about speaking with his wife.

671
00:50:07,781 --> 00:50:12,941
And this also shows us, that even though these men stayed behind, their hearts were alive

672
00:50:13,430 --> 00:50:18,898
because the Munafiq(منافق), he stays behind and doesn't care about it, doesn't even think about it.

673
00:50:19,246 --> 00:50:21,057
He thinks that he has done the right thing.

674
00:50:21,303 --> 00:50:23,470
He believes that he has done the wise thing.

675
00:50:23,706 --> 00:50:27,915
He thinks that he is intelligent and smart he didn't get himself into trouble.

676
00:50:28,231 --> 00:50:29,491
That's how the Munafiq(منافق) thinks.

677
00:50:30,018 --> 00:50:34,505
But the believer realizes the mistake because his heart is awake.

678
00:50:35,040 --> 00:50:38,842
And even though he has committed the mistake it's burning him, deep inside

679
00:50:39,339 --> 00:50:41,512
he's been weeping for 40 days.

680
00:50:42,078 --> 00:50:46,597
فَقَالَ لِي بَعْضُ أَهْلِي لَوْ اسْتَأْذَنْتَ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي امْرَأَتِكَ

681
00:50:46,803 --> 00:50:49,589
كَمَا أَذِنَ لِامْرَأَةِ هِلَالِ بْنِ أُمَيَّةَ أَنْ تَخْدُمَهُ

682
00:50:49,896 --> 00:50:54,024
 فَقُلْتُ وَاللَّهِ لَا أَسْتَأْذِنُ فِيهَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَمَا يُدْرِينِي مَا يَقُولُ

683
00:50:54,276 --> 00:50:57,911
 رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ إِذَا اسْتَأْذَنْتُهُ فِيهَا وَأَنَا رَجُلٌ شَابٌّ

684
00:50:58,140 --> 00:50:59,706
Some of my family members was saying;

685
00:50:59,746 --> 00:51:03,620
Why don't you ask Rasool Allah ﷺ to allow your wife to stay with you.

686
00:51:03,905 --> 00:51:06,645
Just like he allowed the wife of Hilal Ibn Ummayyah(هلال ابن اميه).

687
00:51:06,762 --> 00:51:10,290
He said: No, I'm not going to do that because I don't know what Rasool Ullah would tell me.

688
00:51:10,412 --> 00:51:11,942
 when I'm a young man.

689
00:51:12,521 --> 00:51:14,545
فَلَبِثْتُ بَعْدَ ذَلِكَ عَشْرَ لَيَالٍ

690
00:51:14,674 --> 00:51:16,051
10 days after that

691
00:51:16,282 --> 00:51:18,042
حَتَّى كَمَلَتْ لَنَا خَمْسُونَ لَيْلَةً

692
00:51:18,355 --> 00:51:20,592
Until we reach total of 50 days,

693
00:51:21,198 --> 00:51:25,399
from the time when Rasool Allah ﷺ, prevented everyone from speaking to us.

694
00:51:25,560 --> 00:51:29,268
فَلَمَّا صَلَّيْتُ صَلَاةَ الْفَجْرِ صُبْحَ خَمْسِينَ لَيْلَةً

695
00:51:29,459 --> 00:51:33,477
When I prayed Salaat Ul Fajr(صلاة الفجر) the morning of the 50th day.

696
00:51:33,630 --> 00:51:35,772
وَأَنَا عَلَى ظَهْرِ بَيْتٍ مِنْ بُيُوتِنَا

697
00:51:36,112 --> 00:51:38,483
I was on the roof of one of my houses.

698
00:51:38,851 --> 00:51:42,706
فَبَيْنَ أَنَا جَالِسٌ عَلَى الْحَالِ الَّتِي ذَكَرَ اللَّهُ

699
00:51:43,016 --> 00:51:47,197
 قَدْ ضَاقَتْ عَلَيَّ نَفْسِي وَضَاقَتْ عَلَيَّ الْأَرْضُ بِمَا رَحُبَتْ

700
00:51:47,295 --> 00:51:53,792
While I was sitting down in the situation, that was described by Allah in Qur'an

701
00:51:54,084 --> 00:51:56,683
that my soul became constrained.

702
00:51:56,881 --> 00:51:59,047
And the whole earth became constraint.

703
00:51:59,071 --> 00:52:02,634
I mean, they were feeling that they're constrained, they were feeling the difficulty,

704
00:52:02,861 --> 00:52:05,504
they are feeling sting of the situation.

705
00:52:05,806 --> 00:52:09,004
 I heard somebody yell out to me.

706
00:52:09,304 --> 00:52:19,586
سَمِعْتُ صَوْتَ صَارِخٍ أَوْفَى عَلَى جَبَلِ سَلْعٍ بِأَعْلَى صَوْتِهِ يَا كَعْبُ بْنَ مَالِكٍ أَبْشِرْ قَالَ فَخَرَرْتُ سَاجِدًا

707
00:52:20,019 --> 00:52:26,103
I heard somebody called me from the mountain of Sallah(سلع), with the peak of his voice.

708
00:52:26,177 --> 00:52:28,635
O Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك) rejoice.

709
00:52:28,913 --> 00:52:30,453
I immediately made Sujood(سجود).

710
00:52:30,775 --> 00:52:32,788
وَعَرَفْتُ أَنْ قَدْ جَاءَ فَرَجٌ

711
00:52:32,981 --> 00:52:36,383
And I knew that the problem has been solved.

712
00:52:36,875 --> 00:52:41,566
وَآذَنَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بِتَوْبَةِ اللَّهِ عَلَيْنَا

713
00:52:41,828 --> 00:52:48,419
And Rasool Allah ﷺ must have been given permission from Allahعَزّوجَلّ,

714
00:52:48,596 --> 00:52:52,100
that he accepts our Taubah(توبة) after Salat-Ul-Fajr(صلاة الفجر).

715
00:52:52,362 --> 00:52:57,136
فَذَهَبَ النَّاسُ يُبَشِّرُونَنَا وَذَهَبَ قِبَلَ صَاحِبَيَّ مُبَشِّرُونَ

716
00:52:57,438 --> 00:53:01,443
So people went out to give us the good news.

717
00:53:01,692 --> 00:53:08,909
Some went out to my two companions, while two men came to give me the glad tidings.

718
00:53:08,973 --> 00:53:14,493
وَرَكَضَ إِلَيَّ رَجُلٌ فَرَسًا وَسَعَى سَاعٍ مِنْ أَسْلَمَ فَأَوْفَى عَلَى الْجَبَلِ

719
00:53:14,590 --> 00:53:16,764
So, two men try to get the news to me.

720
00:53:17,010 --> 00:53:20,646
One of them climb the mountain while the other one took a horse.

721
00:53:21,095 --> 00:53:27,305
But the sound was faster to reach to me, then the man on horseback.

722
00:53:27,980 --> 00:53:38,399
فَلَمَّا جَاءَنِي الَّذِي سَمِعْتُ صَوْتَهُ يُبَشِّرُنِي نَزَعْتُ لَهُ ثَوْبَيَّ فَكَسَوْتُهُ إِيَّاهُمَا بِبُشْرَاهُ وَاللَّهِ مَا أَمْلِكُ غَيْرَهُمَا يَوْمَئِذٍ

723
00:53:38,626 --> 00:53:43,209
It was the tradition when somebody gives you a good news that you give him a gift.

724
00:53:43,642 --> 00:53:49,045
So, Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك) said: The one who, I heard him from the mountain he came to me.

725
00:53:49,249 --> 00:53:54,897
So, I gave him my two cloaks and I had nothing but them

726
00:53:55,134 --> 00:54:01,211
and then I had to borrow two other pieces of garment to go and meet Rasool Allah ﷺ.

727
00:54:02,099 --> 00:54:06,967
وَاسْتَعَرْتُ ثَوْبَيْنِ فَلَبِسْتُهُمَا وَانْطَلَقْتُ إِلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ

728
00:54:07,229 --> 00:54:12,055
So, I borrowed two garments and I put them on, and went to Rasool Allah ﷺ and rushed to him.

729
00:54:12,276 --> 00:54:20,113
فَيَتَلَقَّانِي النَّاسُ فَوْجًا فَوْجًا يُهَنُّونِي بِالتَّوْبَةِ يَقُولُونَ لِتَهْنِكَ تَوْبَةُ اللَّهِ عَلَيْكَ

730
00:54:20,601 --> 00:54:23,971
And then people were meeting me in groups,

731
00:54:24,365 --> 00:54:30,028
all greeting me and congratulating me with the Taubah(توبه) of Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

732
00:54:30,351 --> 00:54:38,970
لِتَهْنِكَ تَوْبَةُ اللَّهِ عَلَيْكَ قَالَ كَعْبٌ حَتَّى دَخَلْتُ الْمَسْجِدَ فَإِذَا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ جَالِسٌ حَوْلَهُ النَّاسُ

733
00:54:39,232 --> 00:54:43,474
 فَقَامَ إِلَيَّ طَلْحَةُ بْنُ عُبَيْدِ اللَّهِ يُهَرْوِلُ حَتَّى صَافَحَنِي وَهَنَّانِي

734
00:54:43,658 --> 00:54:48,756
وَاللَّهِ مَا قَامَ إِلَيَّ رَجُلٌ مِنْ الْمُهَاجِرِينَ غَيْرَهُ وَلَا أَنْسَاهَا لِطَلْحَةَ

735
00:54:48,780 --> 00:54:52,471
and then he went into the Masjid(مسجد), and then Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك) says;

736
00:54:52,764 --> 00:54:56,266
قَالَ كَعْبٌ فَلَمَّا سَلَّمْتُ عَلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ

737
00:54:56,527 --> 00:55:05,649
قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَهُوَ يَبْرُقُ وَجْهُهُ مِنْ السُّرُورِ أَبْشِرْ بِخَيْرِ يَوْمٍ مَرَّ عَلَيْكَ مُنْذُ وَلَدَتْكَ أُمُّكَ

738
00:55:06,455 --> 00:55:08,828
When I went to Rasool Allah ﷺ and gave him Salam(سلام),

739
00:55:09,050 --> 00:55:13,831
Rasool Allah ﷺ told me while, his face was beaming with happiness,

740
00:55:14,172 --> 00:55:20,457
rejoice with the best day ever since your mother gave birth to you.

741
00:55:20,797 --> 00:55:25,543
Rasool Allah ﷺ was telling Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك) today is the best day for you,

742
00:55:25,749 --> 00:55:27,680
since the day you were born.

743
00:55:28,051 --> 00:55:31,092
قَالَ قُلْتُ أَمِنْ عِنْدِكَ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ

744
00:55:31,386 --> 00:55:33,678
Is this from you, or from Allah?

745
00:55:33,886 --> 00:55:35,533
قَالَ لَا بَلْ مِنْ عِنْدِ اللَّهِ

746
00:55:35,558 --> 00:55:39,351
No, this is from Allah, this came down from Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

747
00:55:40,018 --> 00:55:47,364
وَكَانَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ إِذَا سُرَّ اسْتَنَارَ وَجْهُهُ حَتَّى كَأَنَّهُ قِطْعَةُ قَمَرٍ وَكُنَّا نَعْرِفُ ذَلِكَ مِنْهُ

748
00:55:47,634 --> 00:55:51,321
When Rasool Allah ﷺ was happy, his face would be like the moon

749
00:55:52,083 --> 00:55:55,789
so Subhaan Allah(سبحان الله) you can see how happy Rasool Allah ﷺ was,

750
00:55:56,004 --> 00:56:01,976
because the acceptance of the Taubah(توبة) of Ka'ab Ibn Malik رضي الله عنه and his two companions.

751
00:56:02,930 --> 00:56:10,507
فَلَمَّا جَلَسْتُ بَيْنَ يَدَيْهِ قُلْتُ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ إِنَّ مِنْ تَوْبَتِي أَنْ أَنْخَلِعَ مِنْ مَالِي صَدَقَةً إِلَى اللَّهِ وَإِلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ

752
00:56:10,884 --> 00:56:15,645
 قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَمْسِكْ عَلَيْكَ بَعْضَ مَالِكَ فَهُوَ خَيْرٌ لَكَ

753
00:56:15,846 --> 00:56:18,523
قُلْتُ فَإِنِّي أُمْسِكُ سَهْمِي الَّذِي بِخَيْبَرَ

754
00:56:18,788 --> 00:56:23,228
And then, I told Rasool Allah ﷺ, part of my repentance would be

755
00:56:23,449 --> 00:56:29,269
that I give away all of my money Sadaqah(صدقه), for Allah and for the Messenger of Allah.

756
00:56:29,657 --> 00:56:34,565
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Leave behind some of your wealth, it is better for you.

757
00:56:34,905 --> 00:56:41,144
He said, I will hold on to my share of Khaybar(خيبر), the Battle of khaybar(خيبر).

758
00:56:41,570 --> 00:56:50,338
فَقُلْتُ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ إِنَّ اللَّهَ إِنَّمَا نَجَّانِي بِالصِّدْقِ وَإِنَّ مِنْ تَوْبَتِي أَنْ لَا أُحَدِّثَ إِلَّا صِدْقًا مَا بَقِيتُ

759
00:56:50,741 --> 00:56:55,969
He said: O Messenger of Allah, Allah has saved me, because of my honesty,

760
00:56:55,993 --> 00:56:57,423
because of speaking the truth.

761
00:56:57,584 --> 00:57:03,831
And part of my repentance is I promise that I will only speak the truth as long as I live.

762
00:57:04,285 --> 00:57:07,528
And when Ka'ab(كعب) is narrating this Hadith(حديث), he said;

763
00:57:07,978 --> 00:57:14,279
And I have been blessed by Allah that since that time, I have not spoken any word but the truth.

764
00:57:14,835 --> 00:57:20,745
Dear brothers and sisters Allahعَزّوجَلّ has revealed the following two Ayaat(آيات) of Surah Taubah(سورة التوبة),

765
00:57:21,063 --> 00:57:24,706
the second Ayah(آية) is about Ka'ab(كعب) and his two companions.

766
00:57:24,896 --> 00:57:25,965
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

767
00:57:26,462 --> 00:57:37,969
لَقَدْ تَابَ اللَّهُ عَلَى النَّبِيِّ وَالْمُهَاجِرِينَ وَالْأَنْصَارِ الَّذِينَ اتَّبَعُوهُ فِي سَاعَةِ الْعُسْرَةِ

768
00:57:38,666 --> 00:57:44,275
الَّذِينَ اتَّبَعُوهُ فِي سَاعَةِ الْعُسْرَةِ مِنْ بَعْدِ

769
00:57:44,561 --> 00:57:52,833
مِنْ بَعْدِ مَا كَادَ يَزِيغُ قُلُوبُ فَرِيقٍ مِنْهُمْ ثُمَّ تَابَ عَلَيْهِمْ

770
00:57:53,235 --> 00:57:57,441
 إِنَّهُ بِهِمْ رَءُوفٌ رَحِيمٌ۝

771
00:57:57,620 --> 00:58:02,919
Allah has already forgiven the Prophet, and the Muhajireen(مهاجرين) and the Ansaar(انصار),

772
00:58:03,288 --> 00:58:06,344
who followed him in the hour of difficulty,

773
00:58:06,621 --> 00:58:13,502
after the hearts of a party of them had almost inclined to doubt and then he forgave them.

774
00:58:13,684 --> 00:58:16,299
Indeed, he was to them kind and merciful.

775
00:58:16,323 --> 00:58:22,323
We talked about this Ayah(آية) before, that it represents the peak of the Muslim community,

776
00:58:22,702 --> 00:58:27,370
and towards the end of the life of Rasool Allah ﷺ, Allahعَزّوجَلّ is accepting their Toba(توبة)

777
00:58:27,945 --> 00:58:29,187
and then Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

778
00:58:29,371 --> 00:58:40,198
وَعَلَى الثَّلَاثَةِ الَّذِينَ خُلِّفُوا حَتَّىٰ إِذَا ضَاقَتْ عَلَيْهِمُ الْأَرْضُ بِمَا رَحُبَتْ

779
00:58:40,569 --> 00:58:48,469
ضَاقَتْ عَلَيْهِمُ الْأَرْضُ بِمَا رَحُبَتْ وَضَاقَتْ عَلَيْهِمْ أَنْفُسُهُمْ

780
00:58:48,855 --> 00:58:56,607
وَظَنُّوا أَنْ لَا مَلْجَأَ مِنَ اللَّهِ إِلَّا إِلَيْهِ

781
00:58:56,907 --> 00:59:05,552
 ثُمَّ تَابَ عَلَيْهِمْ لِيَتُوبُوا ۚ إِنَّ اللَّهَ هُوَ التَّوَّابُ الرَّحِيمُ۝

782
00:59:06,103 --> 00:59:11,521
And he also forgave, the three, who were left behind and regretted their error,

783
00:59:11,799 --> 00:59:19,767
to the point that the earth closed in, on them, in spite of its vastness, and their souls confined them

784
00:59:20,061 --> 00:59:25,028
 and they were certain that there is no refuge from Allah except in Him.

785
00:59:25,313 --> 00:59:28,454
Look at the description, and their souls confined them,

786
00:59:28,479 --> 00:59:30,933
as it, was like they were prisoners, even though they were free.

787
00:59:31,659 --> 00:59:35,170
Allah says, Then He turned to them, so they could repent.

788
00:59:35,439 --> 00:59:39,313
Indeed, Allah is the Accepting of repentance, the Merciful.

789
00:59:39,950 --> 00:59:47,007
So Allahعَزّوجَلّ has accepted the Toubah(توبة) of Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك) and his two companions.

790
00:59:47,230 --> 00:59:54,597
While, let's see what Allah said about the ones, who gave convincing excuses and lied.

791
00:59:54,907 --> 00:59:59,472
Allah says about them, in verse 95, and 96, of Surah Taubah(سورة التوبة).

792
00:59:59,820 --> 01:00:07,952
سَيَحْلِفُونَ بِاللَّهِ لَكُمْ إِذَا انْقَلَبْتُمْ إِلَيْهِمْ لِتُعْرِضُوا عَنْهُمْ

793
01:00:08,332 --> 01:00:12,189
فَأَعْرِضُوا عَنْهُمْ ۖ إِنَّهُمْ رِجْسٌ

794
01:00:12,326 --> 01:00:20,767
وَمَأْوَاهُمْ جَهَنَّمُ جَزَاءً بِمَا كَانُوا يَكْسِبُونَ۝

795
01:00:21,044 --> 01:00:24,719
 يَحْلِفُونَ لَكُمْ لِتَرْضَوْا عَنْهُمْ

796
01:00:25,078 --> 01:00:34,118
فَإِنْ تَرْضَوْا عَنْهُمْ فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ لَا يَرْضَىٰ عَنِ الْقَوْمِ الْفَاسِقِينَ۝

797
01:00:34,388 --> 01:00:39,964
They will swear by Allah to you, when you returned to them, that you would leave them alone.

798
01:00:39,988 --> 01:00:42,738
So, leave them alone, indeed, they are evil,

799
01:00:43,214 --> 01:00:48,742
and their refuge is hell as recompense for what they have been earning,

800
01:00:49,656 --> 01:00:53,289
they swear to you, so that you might be satisfied with them.

801
01:00:53,520 --> 01:00:55,750
But if you should be satisfied with them,

802
01:00:55,957 --> 01:01:01,609
indeed Allah is not satisfied with a defiantly disobedient, people.

803
01:01:02,038 --> 01:01:07,131
You can see the consequences of truth and the consequences of lying.

804
01:01:08,361 --> 01:01:13,621
We will close with some benefits mentioned by Ibn-Al-Qayyim(إبن القيم), in his book Zaad Al Ma'ad(زاد المعاد),

805
01:01:14,080 --> 01:01:14,811
He says;

806
01:01:14,901 --> 01:01:17,225
جَوَازُ إخْبَارِ الرّجُلِ عَنْ تَفْرِيطِهِ

807
01:01:17,250 --> 01:01:21,471
It is allowed for a person to speak about his shortcomings

808
01:01:21,495 --> 01:01:26,088
because we know that in Islam, you're not supposed to speak about your sins.

809
01:01:26,483 --> 01:01:29,534
As long as Allah has given you Sitr(ستر), as long as they are concealed,

810
01:01:29,749 --> 01:01:30,889
you should keep them concealed.

811
01:01:31,159 --> 01:01:35,470
However, here we see that Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك) spoke about some of his shortcomings.

812
01:01:35,708 --> 01:01:39,035
Why? Because there is a benefit in that, because they were known.

813
01:01:39,472 --> 01:01:43,147
And there's a benefit, there are lessons to be learned.

814
01:01:43,424 --> 01:01:48,275
So, he spoke about and he was honest about it, in this narration, and second.

815
01:01:48,514 --> 01:01:50,109
جَوَازُ مَدْحِ الرّجُلِ نَفْسَهُ

816
01:01:50,715 --> 01:01:57,312
It is allowed for a person to praise himself or speak about some good things about himself.

817
01:01:57,980 --> 01:02:01,152
However, this is restricted, this is not open ended because we know that

818
01:02:01,453 --> 01:02:05,551
a person is not supposed to praise themselves or speak about their good,

819
01:02:05,898 --> 01:02:11,866
however, we see here that Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك) did speak about some of the good that he has done.

820
01:02:11,938 --> 01:02:16,204
For example, when he mentioned that he has been in every battle of Rasool Ullah, with the exception of Badr(بدر)

821
01:02:16,395 --> 01:02:21,919
and that he attended Al-Aqabah(العقبة), Bay'ah Tul Aqabah(بيعةالعقبة), but Ibn Qayyim(ابن القيم) says;

822
01:02:21,944 --> 01:02:27,032
جَوَازُ مَدْحِ الْإِنْسَانِ نَفْسَهُ بِمَا فِيهِ مِنْ الْخَيْرِ إذَا لَمْ يَكُنْ عَلَى سَبِيلِ الْفَخْرِ وَالتّرَفّعِ

823
01:02:27,208 --> 01:02:33,583
It is allowed, as long as it's not done out of pride and elevating the status of oneself.

824
01:02:34,126 --> 01:02:36,517
بَيْعَةُ الْعَقَبَةِ مِنْ أَفْضَلِ مَشَاهِدِ الصّحَابَةِ

825
01:02:36,764 --> 01:02:44,865
That the pledge of Al-Aqabah(العقبة) is one of the best events of the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم

826
01:02:45,262 --> 01:02:47,971
 because he used to see it equal to Badr(بدر).

827
01:02:48,558 --> 01:02:51,399
الْمُبَادَرَةُ إلَى انْتِهَازِ فُرْصَةِ الطّاعَةِ

828
01:02:51,424 --> 01:02:53,871
And this is one of the most important lessons that Ibn Qayyim(ابن القيم) mentions,

829
01:02:54,328 --> 01:02:59,866
hasten, and take advantage of opportunities of good that open up for you.

830
01:03:00,626 --> 01:03:05,935
Brothers and sisters, Allahعَزّوجَلّ at some moments of your life

831
01:03:06,212 --> 01:03:10,963
would open up for you doors of opportunity to do good.

832
01:03:11,374 --> 01:03:16,956
These doors of opportunity come and go and sometimes if they go, they go for good.

833
01:03:17,523 --> 01:03:21,187
And if you don't take advantage of them, you missed them forever.

834
01:03:21,831 --> 01:03:25,724
Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك) had an opportunity that opened up for him

835
01:03:25,811 --> 01:03:27,874
 to participate in the Tabook(تبوك) and he missed it.

836
01:03:28,422 --> 01:03:30,906
So, one of the important lessons is because he says,

837
01:03:30,946 --> 01:03:31,778
يَالَيْتَنِي فَعَلْتُ

838
01:03:31,817 --> 01:03:33,095
I wished that I have done so.

839
01:03:33,571 --> 01:03:37,066
Do not sit behind and then say, I wish that I have done so.

840
01:03:37,483 --> 01:03:43,405
Take advantage of the good that comes to you, from Allah.

841
01:03:43,682 --> 01:03:50,883
And sometimes, if you reject these opportunities, the consequences could be very bad.

842
01:03:51,317 --> 01:03:54,470
 Allahعَزّوجَلّ says in verse 24 Surah Al-Anfaal(سورة الانفال)

843
01:03:54,740 --> 01:04:04,921
يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا اسْتَجِيبُوا لِلَّهِ وَلِلرَّسُولِ إِذَا دَعَاكُمْ لِمَا يُحْيِيكُمْ

844
01:04:05,417 --> 01:04:16,497
وَاعْلَمُوا أَنَّ اللَّهَ يَحُولُ بَيْنَ الْمَرْءِ وَقَلْبِهِ وَأَنَّهُ إِلَيْهِ تُحْشَرُونَ۝

845
01:04:16,735 --> 01:04:21,372
O you, who have believed respond to Allah and His Messenger

846
01:04:21,551 --> 01:04:24,521
when he calls you to that which gives you life.

847
01:04:25,084 --> 01:04:28,755
And know that Allah intervenes between a man and his heart

848
01:04:29,023 --> 01:04:31,105
and that to Him you will be gathered.

849
01:04:31,375 --> 01:04:35,962
Allah may intervene between you and your heart and prevent you from joining the next time.

850
01:04:36,396 --> 01:04:38,954
Don't delay, don't stay behind.

851
01:04:39,171 --> 01:04:42,004
Take advantage of the opportunities that open up for you.

852
01:04:42,402 --> 01:04:49,877
يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا اسْتَجِيبُوا لِلَّهِ وَلِلرَّسُولِ إِذَا دَعَاكُمْ لِمَا يُحْيِيكُمْ ۖ وَاعْلَمُوا أَنَّ اللَّهَ يَحُولُ بَيْنَ الْمَرْءِ وَقَلْبِهِ

853
01:04:50,545 --> 01:04:52,953
And Allahعَزّوجَلّ says in Surah Al-An'aam(سورة ألانعام) verse 110.

854
01:04:53,168 --> 01:05:06,918
وَنُقَلِّبُ أَفْئِدَتَهُمْ وَأَبْصَارَهُمْ كَمَا لَمْ يُؤْمِنُوا بِهِ أَوَّلَ مَرَّةٍ وَنَذَرُهُمْ فِي طُغْيَانِهِمْ يَعْمَهُونَ۝

855
01:05:07,531 --> 01:05:11,746
And we will turn away their hearts and their eyes,

856
01:05:12,031 --> 01:05:15,453
just as they refused to believe in it, the first time,

857
01:05:15,644 --> 01:05:20,306
the first time they refused, Allah is turning away their hearts and their eyes.

858
01:05:20,818 --> 01:05:22,720
Subhaan Allah(سبحان الله), we need to be very careful.

859
01:05:23,522 --> 01:05:24,794
And Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

860
01:05:25,032 --> 01:05:34,653
فَلَمَّا زَاغُوا أَزَاغَ اللَّهُ قُلُوبَهُمْ ۚ وَاللَّهُ لَا يَهْدِي الْقَوْمَ الْفَاسِقِينَ۝

861
01:05:35,055 --> 01:05:39,547
And when they deviated, an opportunity of truth opened up, and they deviated,

862
01:05:40,051 --> 01:05:43,991
when they deviated, Allah caused their hearts to deviate.

863
01:05:44,707 --> 01:05:47,731
In verse 115, Surah Taubah(سورة التوبة).

864
01:05:48,030 --> 01:05:55,185
وَمَا كَانَ اللَّهُ لِيُضِلَّ قَوْمًا بَعْدَ إِذْ هَدَاهُمْ حَتَّىٰ

865
01:05:55,430 --> 01:06:00,279
حَتَّىٰ يُبَيِّنَ لَهُمْ مَا يَتَّقُونَ ۚ

866
01:06:00,429 --> 01:06:05,033
إِنَّ اللَّهَ بِكُلِّ شَيْءٍ عَلِيمٌ۝

867
01:06:05,253 --> 01:06:07,836
And Allah would not let the people stray,

868
01:06:08,063 --> 01:06:13,057
after He has guided them, until He makes clear to them, what they should avoid.?

869
01:06:13,225 --> 01:06:17,655
So, Allah makes clear to them what they should avoid, they were given the opportunity of good

870
01:06:17,882 --> 01:06:19,893
indeed Allah is knowing of all things.

871
01:06:20,467 --> 01:06:23,744
So, they were given the opportunity of good, they turned away from it

872
01:06:24,191 --> 01:06:25,939
and then Allah would lead them astray.

873
01:06:26,613 --> 01:06:27,407
 Next lesson;

874
01:06:27,544 --> 01:06:35,450
لَمْ يَكُنْ يَتَخَلّفُ عَنْهُ صَلّى اللّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلّمَ إلّا مُنَافِقٌ أَوْ مَعْذُورٌ أَوْ مَنْ خَلّفَهُ النّبِيّ صَلّى اللّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلّمَ

875
01:06:35,997 --> 01:06:40,290
Ibn Qayyim(ابن القيم) says; The only ones who stayed behind are the Munafiqeen(منافقين)

876
01:06:40,790 --> 01:06:47,351
or the ones, who are excused or the ones who are appointed to stay behind by Rasool Allah ﷺ.

877
01:06:47,895 --> 01:06:52,231
So it's a sign of Nifaaq(نفاق) not to participate, in fighting Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

878
01:06:52,821 --> 01:06:59,024
جَوَازُ الطّعْنِ فِي الرّجُلِ بِمَا يَغْلِبُ عَلَى اجْتِهَادِ الطّاعِنِ حَمِيّةً أَوْ ذَبّا عَنْ اللّهِ وَرَسُولِهِ

879
01:06:59,263 --> 01:07:03,993
It's allowed to speak against the person if it is out of Ijtihaad(إجتحاد)

880
01:07:04,450 --> 01:07:07,205
for the sake of defending Allah and His Messenger.

881
01:07:07,369 --> 01:07:09,274
And this is what the scholars of Hadith(حديث) used to do,

882
01:07:09,313 --> 01:07:11,304
when they would speak about some of the narrator's,

883
01:07:11,534 --> 01:07:15,460
it is because they want to protect the religion of Allah, protect the Hadith(حديث) of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

884
01:07:15,688 --> 01:07:19,508
So, the man of Bannu Salamah(بنو سلمه), when he spoke against Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك), that was the intention.

885
01:07:20,286 --> 01:07:24,305
And it is also allowed to respond back when you think that the person is good,

886
01:07:24,715 --> 01:07:26,182
like Muadh Ibn Jabal(معاذ ابن جبل) did.

887
01:07:27,100 --> 01:07:28,478
الْحُكْمُ بِالظّاهِرِ

888
01:07:28,717 --> 01:07:30,918
We judged according to what is apparent.

889
01:07:31,446 --> 01:07:34,305
تَرْكُ رَدّ السّلَامِ عَلَى مَنْ أَحْدَثَ حَدَثًا

890
01:07:34,621 --> 01:07:41,405
It is allowed to refuse to answer back Salam(سلام) for a person, who has committed Hadaf(حدف),

891
01:07:41,660 --> 01:07:47,536
if a person, who has done a Bid'ah(بدعة) or great sin and you're refusing to answer back his Salaam(سلام).

892
01:07:47,840 --> 01:07:52,127
In order to reprimand the person as a Naseeha(نصيحه) for them.

893
01:07:52,353 --> 01:07:57,747
Then it is allowed because the Muslims, and Rasool Allah ﷺ would not responding back to Salam(سلام) of Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك),

894
01:07:57,795 --> 01:07:59,861
now this should not be carried too far.

895
01:08:00,096 --> 01:08:01,856
Whenever you have a disagreement with the person,

896
01:08:02,071 --> 01:08:05,476
you start finding out what mistakes they did and then

897
01:08:05,965 --> 01:08:11,394
you use that as a scapegoat to not speaking to the person, and not giving Salaam(سلام),

898
01:08:11,663 --> 01:08:16,315
this is obviously, there are some rules and regulations that govern this.

899
01:08:17,342 --> 01:08:19,165
.تَوْفِيقُ اللّهِ لِكَعْبٍ وَصَاحِبَيْهِ

900
01:08:19,189 --> 01:08:25,199
Allah has guided Ka'ab(كعب) and his two companions and that is because of their truth.

901
01:08:25,408 --> 01:08:27,000
جَوَازُ الْهَجْرِ لِلتّأْدِيبِ

902
01:08:27,040 --> 01:08:33,199
It is allowed to boycott a person if it is done as a Naseeha(نصيحه), as an advice for them

903
01:08:33,506 --> 01:08:36,625
to leave a particular sin or particular Bid'ah(بدعة).

904
01:08:37,480 --> 01:08:39,934
التّنَكّرُ وَالْوَحْشَةُ دَلِيلٌ عَلَى حَيَاةِ الْقَلْبِ

905
01:08:40,399 --> 01:08:42,797
When you feel pain in your heart

906
01:08:43,848 --> 01:08:49,557
and when you feel forsaken, that is a sign of a heart that is alive.

907
01:08:49,888 --> 01:08:53,060
However, a person, who is a Munafiq(منافق) he doesn't feel that.

908
01:08:53,166 --> 01:08:57,364
Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك) and his companions, they felt the effect of the boycott

909
01:08:57,923 --> 01:09:01,277
and they felt difference in the way people were treating them.

910
01:09:01,500 --> 01:09:04,030
But with the Munafiq(منافق) they don't care, it doesn't matter to them.

911
01:09:05,128 --> 01:09:07,450
دُخُولُ دَارِ الصّاحِبِ مِنْ غَيْرِ إذْن

912
01:09:07,985 --> 01:09:11,495
You can enter the house of your friends without his permission

913
01:09:11,867 --> 01:09:15,249
as long as you know that he does not mind that

914
01:09:15,713 --> 01:09:19,754
because Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك) climbed the wall, and entered the house of Abu Qatadah(ابو قتادة).

915
01:09:19,778 --> 01:09:24,383
Obviously this is if, you're not going to end up seeing something that is Haraam, you know,

916
01:09:24,893 --> 01:09:27,762
I mean, when Ka'ab(كعب) entered into the house of Abu Qatadah(ابو قتاده),

917
01:09:27,977 --> 01:09:31,432
obviously there won't be any woman without their hijab(حجاب) or something.

918
01:09:31,787 --> 01:09:34,769
So, we're talking about for example, your friend is a bachelor and

919
01:09:35,179 --> 01:09:38,549
you know that he wouldn't mind you, entering into his house and he could do so.

920
01:09:39,475 --> 01:09:41,859
كَانَ سُجُودُ الشّكْرِ مِنْ عَادَةِ الصّحَابَةِ

921
01:09:42,293 --> 01:09:45,902
It was the habit of the Sahabah to make Sujood(سجود) of thanks,

922
01:09:45,926 --> 01:09:49,241
when they would receive a good news, it is something that you're allowed to do,

923
01:09:49,621 --> 01:09:52,333
when you receive good news to make a Sujood(سجود) to Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

924
01:09:52,540 --> 01:09:54,806
.إتْلَافُ مَا يُخْشَى مِنْهُ الْمَضَرّةُ فِي الدّينِ

925
01:09:55,033 --> 01:09:59,473
Destroyed the things that you believe are going to harm you in your religion.

926
01:10:00,086 --> 01:10:04,824
And this is because Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك) destroyed the letter that he received from the king of Ghassan(غسَّان).

927
01:10:05,126 --> 01:10:07,802
.يَوْمُ تَوْبَةِ الْمُسْلِمِ خَيْرُ الْأَيّامِ

928
01:10:07,962 --> 01:10:10,703
The day of your repentance is your best day.

929
01:10:11,269 --> 01:10:14,267
سُرُورُهُ صَلّى اللّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلّمَ بِتَوْبَةِ اللّهِ عَلَى الْمُخَلّفِينَ

930
01:10:14,740 --> 01:10:16,321
The happiness that Rasool Allah ﷺ

931
01:10:16,361 --> 01:10:22,574
 and the pleasure that Rasool Allah ﷺ had when he knew that Allah has forgiven the ones who stayed behind,

932
01:10:22,598 --> 01:10:26,664
and this shows you the care that Rasool Allah ﷺ had for the Ummah(امة).

933
01:10:26,919 --> 01:10:28,781
اسْتِحْبَابُ الصّدَقَةِ عِنْدَ التّوْبَةِ

934
01:10:28,806 --> 01:10:33,009
When you make repentance it is good to give out Sadaqah(صدقه) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله),

935
01:10:33,471 --> 01:10:35,879
so when you repent from a sin, give out Sadaqah(صدقه)

936
01:10:36,258 --> 01:10:42,378
and then he finally closes with the virtues of truth and the virtues of Taubah(توبه).

937
01:10:42,523 --> 01:10:47,993
This the end of the great, wonderful story of Ka'ab Ibn Malik رضي الله عنه.

938
01:10:48,325 --> 01:10:52,013
I would suggest that you go back to Bukhari(بخاريْ) and read the Hadith(حديث) again,

939
01:10:52,267 --> 01:10:54,890
and think about it and thinking about its implications.

940
01:10:55,405 --> 01:11:01,866
We ask Allahعَزّوجَلّ to guide us to the truth and to show us the truth and make us, of the ones who follow it.

941
01:11:02,063 --> 01:11:06,277
صَلَّى الله عَلى سَيَّدِنَا محمد وَعَلى اَلِهِ وَ صَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرًا

942
01:11:06,573 --> 01:11:09,226
اَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكُمْ وَرَحْمةُ الله وَبَرَكَاتُه’

